},"authoredDate":"2026-09-04T18:39:32Z","committedDate":"2026-09-04T18:39:32Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"zakaria-rab","providerType":"User"},"email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:30:57.215Z","repositoryId":1356302738,"sha":"4dd674fddfcee19f0f8e9891be3cb5c8f2ed9e35"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"zakaria-rab","providerType":"User"},"email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"zakaria-rab"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-04T00:31:02Z","committedDate":"2026-09-04T00:31:02Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"zakaria-rab","providerType":"User"},"email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"zakaria-rab"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:30:57.215Z","repositoryId":1356302738,"sha":"efcf3741a6d9c5ef45349095edb85f862460dc33"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"zakaria-rab","providerType":"User"},"email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"zakaria-rab"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-03T18:26:36Z","committedDate":"2026-09-03T18:26:36Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:30:57.215Z","repositoryId":1356302738,"sha":"d7ae1b6868dc2ab67e62dbd383a783190e387b3d"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:30:57.215Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/ffafaadb8403862e4cdbb119e239e49d57924f2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:42:42Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:42:42Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"fix: look the served prefix up by package name, not by elimination\n\nThe derivation added an hour ago took \"the application that isn''t the shell\",\nwhich is right in this repo today and wrong as soon as the group has two apps.\n\nvercel.json builds with `vercel microfrontends pull`, which replaces\nmicrofrontends.json with the group''s authoritative copy — and that copy lists\nevery application in the group, not just this one. Demonstrated against a\nconfig listing glass-ui-room-booking-board before glass-ui-app1:\n\n  old logic (first non-shell) picks  /apps/room-booking-board\n  new logic (by package name) picks  /apps/app1\n\nSo this app would have prefixed every browser request with a sibling''s slug:\nrequests routed to a different app entirely, answered by whatever schema that\napp has. Invisible locally, because the committed config lists only this app —\nit would have appeared the first time a second app joined the group, which has\nalready happened.\n\nKeyed on package.json name because that is the key the platform itself matches\non: withMicrofrontends fails with \"Could not find microfrontends configuration\nfor application <name>\" when the two disagree, and rename-app.ts rewrites the\npackage name and the application key together. Looking up a name that must\nalready agree is safer than inferring one that need not.\n\nAlso throws with a usable message when the lookup misses, rather than\nreturning undefined and composing \"undefined/api/graphql\".\n\nSame fix is on zakaria-rab/glass-ui-room-booking-board@3c08063, which is where\nthis was found: that app was stamped before the browser-path fix existed, so it\ncarried the unprefixed /api/graphql and every save failed with\n`Unknown type \"NewPatient\"` from the shell''s schema. Stamped apps do not\ninherit template fixes retroactively — each existing app needs this applied.\n\nVerified with the multi-app config in place: 7 tests pass, build clean, and\nBASE_PATH resolves to /apps/app1 rather than the sibling''s slug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8254740ff7a5ba5decd989557001d26a23620bf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/8254740ff7a5ba5decd989557001d26a23620bf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/ffafaadb8403862e4cdbb119e239e49d57924f2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/ffafaadb8403862e4cdbb119e239e49d57924f2a","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGZmYWZhYWRiODQwMzg2MmU0Y2RiYjExOWUyMzllNDlkNTc5MjRmMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4","sha":"9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4"}],"sha":"ffafaadb8403862e4cdbb119e239e49d57924f2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/ffafaadb8403862e4cdbb119e239e49d57924f2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:25:50Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:25:50Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"fix: derive the served prefix from the file provisioning can''t get wrong\n\nFollow-up to the previous commit, which fixed the symptom and broke stamping.\n\nPointing next.config.ts at an imported BASE_PATH removed the literal that\nprovisioning rewrites. rename-app.ts does that with\n`text.replace(/basePath:\\s*\"[^\"]*\"/, ...)`, and a regex that does not match\nreplaces nothing and reports nothing — so every future stamped app would have\nkept /apps/app1 in next.config.ts while microfrontends.json correctly claimed\n/apps/<its-own-slug>. The app would serve a path the group never sends it: 404\neverywhere through the shell, working perfectly at its own URL, which is the\nexact failure that rule''s comment says it exists to prevent. Silent in the\ntemplate, visible only on the second app anyone stamps.\n\nSo the prefix is now read from microfrontends.json, which provisioning rewrites\nby parsing rather than by regex, and next.config.ts keeps its literal with a\ncomment saying why it must stay one. One source of truth, and it is the copy\nthat cannot be silently missed.\n\nsrc/lib/base-path.test.ts asserts the two agree, and fails loudly if the\nliteral is ever refactored into an expression again — it caught exactly that\nwhile this change was being written, which is the argument for it existing.\n\nVerified by simulating a real stamp rather than reasoning about it: renamed\npackage.json, microfrontends.json and next.config.ts to glass-ui-claims-triage\nthe way rename-app.ts does, then built and ran it. /apps/claims-triage returns\n200 with four rows server-rendered, the client bundle composes\n/apps/claims-triage/api/graphql from the derived value, a mutation on that path\nsucceeds, and /apps/app1 correctly 404s. Restored to the template''s own slug\nafterwards.\n\nOne thing that simulation surfaced: renaming only microfrontends.json fails the\nbuild outright with \"Could not find microfrontends configuration for\napplication glass-ui-app1\", because withMicrofrontends matches on the\npackage.json name. Loud rather than silent, and rename-app.ts already rewrites\nboth — worth knowing that the two are coupled.\n\nTemplate still serves /apps/app1: page 200, four rows, add and remove both\nworking through the prefixed path. 7 tests, lint and build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"886fafbfcc7be2c5c0fe53f8c2ee8ae4eeeea807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/886fafbfcc7be2c5c0fe53f8c2ee8ae4eeeea807"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKDk5MDVkYmRmYTQwMzE5ODBiMGZkODFmNGNjMzQ0N2Y5NzE3YTViYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97","sha":"f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97"}],"sha":"9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/9905dbdfa4031980b0fd81f4cc3447f9717a5ba4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:20:50Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:20:50Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"fix: prefix the browser''s GraphQL path, so mutations reach this app\n\nAdding a patient failed with `Unknown type \"NewPatient\". Cannot query field\n\"addPatient\" on type \"Mutation\"` — an error from a schema that is not ours.\n\nbasePath arrived in d1778eb because Vercel Microfrontends does not strip the\nmatched prefix, so this app has to serve /apps/app1 itself. basePath teaches\nNext''s routing and <Link> about that prefix and does not touch `fetch`, so the\nbrowser kept posting to a root-relative /api/graphql. Two things follow, and\nthe second is why the error was confusing rather than obvious:\n\n- On this app''s own origin that path is a 404; the handler now lives at\n  /apps/app1/api/graphql.\n- Through the group it is worse than a 404. Microfrontends forwards any path an\n  app has not claimed to the default application, and this app claims only\n  /apps/app1 and /apps/app1/:path*. So the request left the app, reached the\n  *shell''s* GraphQL endpoint, and was answered by a schema that has apps and\n  buildRequests and no patients at all. Hence a type error naming our input\n  type, from a server that has never heard of it.\n\nReads were unaffected throughout, which is what made this look like a backend\nthat half-existed: server components execute the schema in-process, so the\ntable rendered four rows while every write failed.\n\nThe prefix now has one definition. src/lib/base-path.ts exports BASE_PATH and\nan appPath() helper; next.config.ts imports it for basePath and the GraphQL\nclient composes its URL from it, so the two cannot drift. The remaining copy of\nthe slug is microfrontends.json, which is JSON and cannot import — noted in the\ncomment as the one that must be kept in step by hand when provisioning stamps\nan app.\n\nAnything else built for the browser needs appPath() for the same reason. The\nrule is in the module''s comment rather than only in this message.\n\nVerified against a production build: the built client bundle contains\n/apps/app1/api/graphql, the page server-renders four rows, and addPatient,\nchangePatient and removePatient all succeed with a mutation over HTTP visible\nto a fresh server render. The bad-date validation still surfaces its own\nmessage. /api/graphql still 404s on this origin, which is correct — that is the\npath the group would have handed to the shell. Seed untouched, 5 tests, lint\nand build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e39408ca68596e2fe1aa06b924d1cf1cd8b8c775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/e39408ca68596e2fe1aa06b924d1cf1cd8b8c775"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGYzZmIxOTYyOTA3M2QzNTA4ODM5ZWI4ZjQ0MjI0YmY2YWU4YjNmOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa","sha":"d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa"}],"sha":"f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/f3fb19629073d3508839eb8f44224bf6ae8b3f97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T16:10:39Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T16:10:39Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"fix: serve the paths microfrontends forwards\n\nMicrofrontends does not strip the matched prefix. An app routed at /apps/<slug>\nmust serve /apps/<slug>, and without basePath every stamped app answers 404\nthrough the group while working perfectly at its own URL — with the 404 page\ncarrying the app''s own asset prefix, so it reads as a routing fault rather than\nan app one.\n\nFound on the first real group member, not by reading the docs.\n\nProvisioning rewrites this to the app''s slug when it stamps a repository.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef9bef182b6f1d84d8cacddcaa131b8d5613c1a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/ef9bef182b6f1d84d8cacddcaa131b8d5613c1a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGQxNzc4ZWI2MjFlMWNlNjAwMmIxMjQ1ZmViNjUxYTJkNGFiMGQ1YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a","sha":"18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a"}],"sha":"d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/d1778eb621e1ce6002b1245feb651a2d4ab0d5aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:28:05Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T03:28:05Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"fix: a stamped app must deploy before it joins the group\n\nThe build command was ''vercel microfrontends pull && next build''. A project is\nnot in a microfrontends group until someone runs ''vercel mf add-to-group'' from\na terminal, and provisioning runs in a serverless function and cannot. So the\npull fails on every newly stamped app, and && meant the whole build failed with\nit — an app that could never deploy at all.\n\nThe pull is now best-effort with the committed microfrontends.json as the\nfallback, which is exactly what that file was committed for. Once the project\njoins the group the pull succeeds and its config wins, so the ordering is right\nin both states rather than only the finished one.\n\nCaught by walking the provisioning sequence before our user pressed the button,\nnot by a failed deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da36255451235157af633aed7f5af1f6f960ecff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/da36255451235157af633aed7f5af1f6f960ecff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKDE4Nzk2ODUzY2M1OGRkMGY4ZjAyNjM4YmM0YjA3ZDQ2ZGU3YjNjN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a","sha":"2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a"}],"sha":"18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/18796853cc58dd0f8f02638bc4b07d46de7b3c7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T02:54:21Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T02:54:21Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"feat: make this app a real microfrontend, not a proxied one\n\nwithMicrofrontends generates the vc-ap-* asset prefix, replacing the\nassetPrefix we derived from VERCEL_URL by hand. Same problem, solved by the\nplatform, and it stops two apps colliding on /_next/* rather than only stopping\none colliding with the shell.\n\nvercel.json pulls the config at build. In a polyrepo the authoritative\nmicrofrontends.json lives in the default application and a build that cannot\nfind it fails outright — verified, not assumed: without it the build dies with\n''Could not find microfrontends configuration for application glass-ui-app1''.\n\nThe committed microfrontends.json exists for a reason worth stating: pnpm build\nin a fresh clone has no Vercel auth and therefore cannot pull, and Open Inspect\nsandboxes run pnpm rather than the Vercel CLI. Gopi asked that any app stamped\nfrom this template be enhanceable locally in Open Inspect, so a build that\nneeds a Vercel login to succeed is not acceptable. On Vercel the pull\noverwrites it.\n\nIts applications key must match the Vercel project name and its routing paths\nmust match the slug. Provisioning rewrites both when it stamps an app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d504824a4d59a56f6177cb447d830c60c166ec17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/d504824a4d59a56f6177cb447d830c60c166ec17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKDJjN2U3M2E1NzdiYTYyNWQ1ZWM0YWIyMzViNDA1NDNhZTZmYjYxN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295","sha":"f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295"}],"sha":"2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/2c7e73a577ba625d5ec4ab235b40543ae6fb617a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:38:19Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:38:19Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"feat: the real Overjet design system, not an approximation of it\n\nEvery app stamped from this template had a hand-rolled 14-token palette with a\n''TODO: replace with an Overjet design-system token'' left on the accent colour.\nSo generated apps looked approximately Overjet, and nothing documented or\nenforced the difference.\n\nNow: src/design/tokens.css copied verbatim from the design system, 75 tokens,\nand a base layer identical to the shell''s. Identical on purpose — an app renders\ninside the portal and standalone at its own URL and must look the same in both.\nDiverging is how an app starts looking almost-Overjet, which is worse than\nlooking unstyled.\n\nThe ad-hoc palette mapped one-for-one onto real tokens, so this is a rename and\nnot a restyle: --oj-accent was already #5100FE, --oj-radius already 12px. One\ngenuine correction — a brand surface now uses --text-on-brand instead of the\ncard colour.\n\ndocs/design.md carries the rules a token file cannot express, each of which has\nbeen got wrong before: warm off-white canvas never white, cards never bordered,\nviolet as the only brand primary, sentence case, tabular numerals where numbers\nalign, verb-first buttons, errors that say how to fix themselves.\n\nForm controls are styled globally, which the shell does not do and should not.\nThe shell has components so its bare elements never appear; an app here has\nnone, so its input, select and button are the real controls someone touches.\nLeft alone they render as browser defaults — correct tokens, wrong look. That\nwas visible in a screenshot and invisible in the build.\n\nRestored the deployment footer classes, which lived in the file that was\nreplaced. Checked every class in the old file survives rather than assuming.\n\nVerified by rendering, not by building: body background resolves to\nrgb(249,247,245).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e57d9793288fabe79b3a7a0b809c8b8762fdc02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/4e57d9793288fabe79b3a7a0b809c8b8762fdc02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGY4MGVjYTQzOGYwNDkzMmNjYzcwNzBkN2M4ODc2ODkzYTJmMmEyOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb","sha":"5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb"}],"sha":"f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/f80eca438f04932ccc7070d7c8876893a2f2a295"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:19:31Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:19:31Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"refactor: the GraphQL tier relays to a source instead of owning the JSON\n\nGopi asked for a Node/GraphQL tier that relays to backend services, with a\nstatic JSON file standing in until the network allows reaching them. The\nresolvers imported that JSON directly, which satisfies \"a GraphQL query reads\ndata from a static file to verify end-to-end connectivity\" and is not a relay\ntier: pointing it at a real service would have meant rewriting every resolver\nrather than adding one file. That distinction is the whole substance of the\nask, and it is why the GKE sandboxes exist.\n\n  before   resolver -> import patients from \"./mocks/patients.json\"\n  after    resolver -> PatientsSource.list() -> static JSON today\n                                             -> an internal service tomorrow\n\n`src/server/patients-source.ts` is the interface and the swap point.\n`StaticPatientsSource` is the only implementation. Resolvers depend on the\ninterface and never on a file, and CLAUDE.md now carries that as a rule — a new\nfield means a source method plus a resolver, never a JSON import in\nsrc/graphql/ — because that is what stops the seam eroding once apps are\nstamped from this template.\n\nEvery method is async although the current implementation is synchronous. An\nHTTP-backed source is unavoidably async, and a sync interface today would mean\nchanging every caller later, which is the rewrite the seam exists to prevent.\n\nNo speculative HTTP client. The env var that would select one is named and\ndocumented and nothing reads it yet; writing that layer now would put an unused\nclient into every stamped app for a service that does not exist.\n\nThis also relocates the in-memory ceiling to where it belongs. It was a\nproperty of the data layer and is now a property of one implementation: the\nwarning about writes vanishing on deploy, on idle and between instances lives\non StaticPatientsSource, which says replace this file rather than the\nresolvers. A template that teaches \"swap the implementation\" is better than one\nthat teaches \"the data layer is in-memory\".\n\nAlso recorded, so it is not re-derived: why this keeps the hand-rolled gql()\nrather than adopting a client library. It matches the shell, so the template\nand the portal teach one pattern, and there was no convention to inherit —\nApollo in insurance-analytics-frontend and its fork, graphql-request in\npnm_platform and devops-triage, hand-rolled in the shell. Four repos, three\nanswers. And that \"a Node.js server\" means this route handler, not a second\nVercel project against a limit Gopi raised himself.\n\nOne deliberate oddity: src/graphql/patients.ts imports the source relatively\nwith an explicit .ts extension rather than through @/. pnpm test runs these\nmodules under plain Node, which reads neither the tsconfig path alias nor\nextensionless specifiers. Type-only imports still use @/ because they are\nerased before Node sees them.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged and verified end to end: four rows server-rendered, a\nmutation over /api/graphql visible to a fresh server render, trimming,\ndefaults, and the blank/bad-date/empty-change/unknown-id errors all identical.\nSeed file untouched. Lint, 5 tests and build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c0210facea7b0a601b5ee0ea7d1415bc9578cdfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/c0210facea7b0a601b5ee0ea7d1415bc9578cdfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKDVhOWZkZDFhNjI2Nzk5MjFkMDA5ZTE5NWZhNzAxZDM5YzgwMDAxYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd","sha":"ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd"}],"sha":"5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/5a9fdd1a62679921d009e195fa701d39c80001bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:05:27Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:05:27Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"docs: say the in-memory store is a shortcut, and why gql() over a client library\n\nTwo things a person stamping an app from this template needs told, neither of\nwhich the code says today.\n\nThe store''s ceiling, out loud. A write lands in one instance and only that\ninstance: gone on the next deploy, gone when the instance goes idle, invisible\nto anyone served by a different one, so two people using the app at once can\nsee different lists. Nothing reports any of that — the mutation returns 200 and\nthe row appears — which is exactly why it has to be written down rather than\ndiscovered. It is the right trade for a schedule of invented patients whose job\nis to show what a Glass UI app looks like, and the wrong one for anything a\nuser expects to find again. Replacing it means replacing one file, since the\nresolvers call five functions and nothing above the GraphQL boundary knows how\nthey are backed.\n\nAlso said plainly, because the two get conflated: a real store is not what\nwould make real patient data acceptable here. Patient records are PHI and do\nnot belong in this repo, its mock JSON, or any deployment of it, whether the\nstore is memory or Postgres.\n\nAnd the client choice, recorded so it is not re-derived. `gql()` is hand-rolled\nand matches the shell, so the template and the portal teach one pattern — the\nconsistency worth having for something ten apps are stamped from. There was no\nconvention to inherit: the org has no single GraphQL client. Apollo in\ninsurance-analytics-frontend and its demo fork, graphql-request in pnm_platform\nand devops-triage, hand-rolled in the shell — four repos, three answers.\n\nRelay was investigated and rejected on the merits, which is worth stating since\na meeting summary appeared to ask for it. Its value is fragments, store\nnormalisation and colocation; this schema has no Node interface, no global IDs\nand no connection types; and a compiler step sits badly in a template that\nagents generate code into. A four-column patient table exercises none of what\nRelay is for.\n\nDocs and comments only — no behaviour change. Lint, test and build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48d4f5897355eda97bcc1bde1651d9797de4f9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/48d4f5897355eda97bcc1bde1651d9797de4f9b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGVjMTFjYWJlOTdmNTUxY2RhNDQxZjhmMDk5MDcyOTA2MWVmZjI1YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def","sha":"d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def"}],"sha":"ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/ec11cabe97f551cda441f8f0990729061eff25bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:35:48Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:39:09Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"feat: a practice-management demo behind a GraphQL boundary\n\nReplaces the Hello World page with a small PMS: a patient schedule you can\nadd to, edit inline and remove. Synthetic data only — fake names and 555\nnumbers — and it must stay that way, because real dental records are PHI and\ndo not belong in a public template.\n\nThe data layer is the shell''s shape, not a new one: graphql-yoga behind\n/api/graphql, SDL in src/graphql/schema.ts, resolvers over JSON in\nsrc/graphql/mocks/, and one gql() in src/lib/graphql-client.ts that executes\nin-process on the server and POSTs from the browser so callers cannot tell\nwhich. Deliberately not Relay: `grep -riE relay` on glass-ui-framework main\nreturns nothing, so Relay would make this template diverge from the shell it\ncomposes into, and its compiler plus babel plugin fights Turbopack for no\ngain at this stage.\n\nFour things that a passing local run cannot see, found by testing the\ndeployed shapes rather than the laptop ones:\n\n- The store must not write its seed back. Vercel function filesystems are\n  read-only outside /tmp, so fs.writeFile into src/graphql/mocks/ works here\n  and 500s on every mutation in production while reads keep succeeding, so\n  the app looks healthy. State is in memory, seeded from JSON.\n- That state has to be pinned to globalThis, not module scope. Next builds\n  the route handler and the page as separate server module graphs, so a\n  module-scope const is evaluated once per graph. Measured: a patient added\n  over /api/graphql left the HTTP store at 5 rows while a fresh server render\n  still saw 4, so a browser mutation then a reload showed the old list with\n  no error anywhere.\n- The page has to call await connection(). Without it Next prerenders it —\n  it touches no request data — and serves the build-time seed for ever.\n  connection() rather than force-dynamic, matching the shell, because segment\n  config would rule out partial prerendering for every app stamped from here.\n- Date.parse(\"2026-02-31\") does not fail, it rolls over to 2026-03-03, so a\n  nonexistent appointment date was accepted silently. Round-tripping the\n  parse back to a string is what rejects it.\n\nCLAUDE.md said three things this makes false, and one it already had wrong:\ndata access no longer goes through the shell''s endpoint, graphql and\ngraphql-yoga are new dependencies, the app is no longer presentational, and\nassetPrefix has been required since b8ad949 despite the rule forbidding it.\nA template whose rules contradict its own code misleads every app stamped\nfrom it, so the rules move with the code.\n\nErrors name what failed and how to fix it, per the design system: a blank\nname, an impossible date, a negative balance, an empty change set and an\nunknown id each say so rather than returning \"Unexpected error.\"\n\nKept: the deployment footer, Vercel Analytics, Inter, the --oj-* tokens, and\nno basePath. pnpm lint, pnpm test (5) and pnpm build all clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba37e7b8bbc8e20a09b03477b810e0407bc51122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/ba37e7b8bbc8e20a09b03477b810e0407bc51122"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGQ4ZDMyNWJhNGNlZjJiZDI1YjhhOTIxYWQ0NDMyOThjNjVhMDNkZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421","sha":"448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421"}],"sha":"d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/d8d325ba4cef2bd25b8a921ad443298c65a03def"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:29:43Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"zakaria-rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T00:29:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(flags): Flagsmith in the template, both halves (#2)\n\n* feat(flags): Flagsmith in the template, both halves\n\nGopi''s redirect was to enhance the template rather than stamp more apps, and a\nflag that only works in the shell reaches no app. So every app provisioned from\nhere now has flags on day one: getFlag() during the render, FlagsProvider\nhydrating the browser, useFlag() in client components. Same SDK on both halves,\nsame module as the shell.\n\nThe browser never calls Flagsmith - the provider is given serverState and no\noptions, so it never inits a connection. No environment key in the bundle, and\nan app works for a user off the Jamf tunnel.\n\nforce-dynamic on the root layout, because otherwise the flag read is evaluated\nonce during next build and baked into a prerendered page: flipping a flag would\nchange nothing until the next deploy, which is not a feature flag.\n\nGive each app its own Flagsmith environment key via FLAGSMITH_ENVIRONMENT_KEY.\nWith no key every flag takes its call-site fallback and the app logs that flags\nare not live.\n\nVerified: pnpm lint, pnpm build, and a production server with no key serves /\nwith a 200 and the loud log.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(flags): connection() instead of force-dynamic, one idiom for the template\n\nSame placement, different mechanism. The shell''s CLAUDE.md already settles\nthis: \"pages that query on the server call `await connection()` first, so the\nregistry is read at request time instead of being frozen into the build\", and\nall three shell pages do it. This template is stamped into every future app, so\nit should teach that idiom rather than a second one.\n\nIt also leaves the segment config alone. A blanket force-dynamic on the root\nlayout would rule out partial prerendering for every route of every app stamped\nfrom here, forever, with nobody re-deciding it.\n\nVerified the route is still dynamic (ƒ, not ○) and that two consecutive\nrequests each read flags rather than serving a frozen build-time value.\n\nRaised by zakariarab-d0, who hit the same prerender problem in parallel work\nand used connection(); agreed on their argument rather than keeping mine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(flags): say what connection() buys here today, which is nothing yet\n\nThe previous comment claimed the partial-prerendering win without saying that\nthis layout does not collect it: with the flag read at the top of a root layout\nand no <Suspense> boundary around it, this app is as all-dynamic as\nforce-dynamic would have made it. What connection() actually preserves is the\noption — Next''s caching guide puts it inside a Suspense-wrapped component so\nthe tree prerenders around the dynamic hole — and the comment now says what\nwould have to change to collect it.\n\nRaised by zakariarab-d0 after we both checked Next 16''s docs; their placement\nhas the same shape and the same unrealised payoff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5d68175ae57bacecf6f48cf319ef6e838d78b4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/e5d68175ae57bacecf6f48cf319ef6e838d78b4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421","verification":{"payload":"tree e5d68175ae57bacecf6f48cf319ef6e838d78b4e\nparent b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e\nauthor zakaria-rab <zakaria.rab@overjet.ai> 1788568183 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788568183 -0700\n\nfeat(flags): Flagsmith in the template, both halves (#2)\n\n* feat(flags): Flagsmith in the template, both halves\n\nGopi''s redirect was to enhance the template rather than stamp more apps, and a\nflag that only works in the shell reaches no app. So every app provisioned from\nhere now has flags on day one: getFlag() during the render, FlagsProvider\nhydrating the browser, useFlag() in client components. Same SDK on both halves,\nsame module as the shell.\n\nThe browser never calls Flagsmith - the provider is given serverState and no\noptions, so it never inits a connection. No environment key in the bundle, and\nan app works for a user off the Jamf tunnel.\n\nforce-dynamic on the root layout, because otherwise the flag read is evaluated\nonce during next build and baked into a prerendered page: flipping a flag would\nchange nothing until the next deploy, which is not a feature flag.\n\nGive each app its own Flagsmith environment key via FLAGSMITH_ENVIRONMENT_KEY.\nWith no key every flag takes its call-site fallback and the app logs that flags\nare not live.\n\nVerified: pnpm lint, pnpm build, and a production server with no key serves /\nwith a 200 and the loud log.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(flags): connection() instead of force-dynamic, one idiom for the template\n\nSame placement, different mechanism. The shell''s CLAUDE.md already settles\nthis: \"pages that query on the server call `await connection()` first, so the\nregistry is read at request time instead of being frozen into the build\", and\nall three shell pages do it. This template is stamped into every future app, so\nit should teach that idiom rather than a second one.\n\nIt also leaves the segment config alone. A blanket force-dynamic on the root\nlayout would rule out partial prerendering for every route of every app stamped\nfrom here, forever, with nobody re-deciding it.\n\nVerified the route is still dynamic (ƒ, not ○) and that two consecutive\nrequests each read flags rather than serving a frozen build-time value.\n\nRaised by zakariarab-d0, who hit the same prerender problem in parallel work\nand used connection(); agreed on their argument rather than keeping mine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(flags): say what connection() buys here today, which is nothing yet\n\nThe previous comment claimed the partial-prerendering win without saying that\nthis layout does not collect it: with the flag read at the top of a root layout\nand no <Suspense> boundary around it, this app is as all-dynamic as\nforce-dynamic would have made it. What connection() actually preserves is the\noption — Next''s caching guide puts it inside a Suspense-wrapped component so\nthe tree prerenders around the dynamic hole — and the comment now says what\nwould have to change to collect it.\n\nRaised by zakariarab-d0 after we both checked Next 16''s docs; their placement\nhas the same shape and the same unrealised payoff.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm2J3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYngQAJD5OSlbxFS/AUBvNSiADXFL\nMegH/L3ujWBAIUxMDts0TJSTO6yfPUpqkzpY6hg8nTvlH3fDcgjof23TAp2rc7Df\ntu7VhXSCutM5rsyiCsAjYY3LaV+ezNNqSa8uXHTl+LnC6QJBZEV4YyPVMnCCsVYF\nqauTv6k+PmtZ0caqx/z+cKj+W9ezZzQRLZqS+tEvHjo7GfRtGcqAKyKrZICKpSfT\n8IdhHpq8M1XPh39T3Ue8OyKPPn99ON4ctFzQMZyhzlT8VXQXYS4DGeBRh5+/jM1c\n1Y1mxheZiwMViOLg7XCkHULMDcZbR7KK8mCSql1kqAx6QPXwhXsA1VYysFG2USe+\n67piQfyCJZ8ZmF2UxixQ8gU8eDnPaaHSn2q1t1QULP8Py37ddN44ms/SGCs9rbdE\ne5iLq8O73Pf9ststksm2/ML2b9s0wpxTuVl5ny5xHGxdJExP7vIMqm2irp8XCuEo\nReZ9tRoPnZyZ96hp05ugl2NjAwCkyqRUGY09Q0PShlVXP5xPelHJ7Jf9OeWK1itl\n5tsCBGEJoXXWVqsoJtrlaZq21k4qeoJzBGc+kCk/trxxiW5adDsW2qSZ91zI4oHF\ncmbI9ikuFQYtFNH/7qPOQU0949Tr1/fLH3Vpl4gVzQsEP3mvIYbu3fFBTMDqOqg2\nGuDrd7yGa2KxinUJvggZ\n=Qld1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T00:29:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKDQ0OGEwY2ZhNGYzMmU3ZDMxNDgzNjQ5MzU3YTVjNDJmYjhiMTE0MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e","sha":"b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e"}],"sha":"448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/448a0cfa4f32e7d31483649357a5c42fb8b11421"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:36:59Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:36:59Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"Zakaria Rab"},"message":"fix: absolute asset URLs, so the shell can serve this app under its own domain\n\nThe shell rewrites /apps/<slug>/* to this app''s deployment, which means this\napp''s HTML is delivered from the shell''s origin. A root-relative /_next/... in\nthat HTML then resolves against the shell, which has no such chunk: every\nscript and stylesheet 404s and the page arrives unstyled and dead. Verified\nagainst a deployed app — 404 through the shell, 200 on the app''s own origin.\n\nassetPrefix makes those references absolute so they load from this deployment\nwhichever origin served the HTML. Vercel''s Microfrontends product generates a\nvc-ap-* prefix to solve exactly this; we are doing Multi-Zones by hand, so we\ndo this by hand too.\n\nDerived from VERCEL_URL rather than written down, so every app and every\npreview points at its own assets with nothing to configure per app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e52eb95af117adbd903d6a5cb59dfbf4f89c983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/5e52eb95af117adbd903d6a5cb59dfbf4f89c983"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e","node_id":"C_kwDOUNeJktoAKGI4YWQ5NDk5MjRkNzA5ZGJjMmE0MzA2MTljM2JjMjEzZWEyOGQ4N2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commit/7c91630bf332a1de6312e48a23223aaa9ac16a2d","sha":"7c91630bf332a1de6312e48a23223aaa9ac16a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/7c91630bf332a1de6312e48a23223aaa9ac16a2d"}],"sha":"b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/b8ad949924d709dbc2a430619c3bc213ea28d87e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323324583?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zakaria-rab","id":323324583,"login":"zakaria-rab","node_id":"U_kgDOE0WKpw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zakaria-rab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/commits/7c91630bf332a1de6312e48a23223aaa9ac16a2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:00:14Z","email":"zakaria.rab@overjet.ai","name":"zakaria-rab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:00:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix Open Inspect sandbox startup: detach the dev server in start.sh (#1)\n\nSame bug as glass-ui-framework#20: the runtime gives .openinspect/start.sh\n120s (START_TIMEOUT_SECONDS) and requires exit 0, killing the script''s whole\nprocess group and failing session startup on timeout. `exec pnpm dev` never\nexits, so sessions died two minutes in with \"Sandbox Failed\".\n\nBackground the dev server, poll :3001, exit 0 once it answers. Also pin the\ninstall to the lockfile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c92e86a5571d3a85c931202a8d03c6c375ef5e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/trees/c92e86a5571d3a85c931202a8d03c6c375ef5e25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zakaria-rab/glass-ui-app1/git/commits/7c91630bf332a1de6312e48a23223aaa9ac16a2d","verification":{"payload":"tree c92e86a5571d3a85c931202a8d03c6c375ef5e25\nparent 4dd674fddfcee19f0f8e9891be3cb5c8f2ed9e35\nauthor zakaria-rab <zakaria.rab@overjet.ai> 1788548414 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788548414 -0700\n\nFix Open Inspect sandbox startup: detach the dev server in start.sh (#1)\n\nSame bug as glass-ui-framework#20: the runtime gives .openinspect/start.sh\n120s (START_TIMEOUT_SECONDS) and requires exit 0, killing the script''s whole\nprocess group and failing session startup on timeout. `exec pnpm dev` never\nexits, so sessions died two minutes in with \"Sandbox Failed\".\n\nBackground the dev server, poll :3001, exit 0 once it answers. Also pin the\ninstall to the lockfile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmxU+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgXUQAJJs1a3aaIMnIq8X9O+q15Ix\nOeqrPCuxyt7lwg8LKSqvViCYn1tjTPiNy0OkEMiZL07FXmnr/qk2ricUB1FYnZVs\nLusX3ayO94j3QjsGUN5/hElxY2y8oE8OLel3x9ERuQT8Gai3lvpbCNnwohuK/ogd\ngFeOQnZ+P9rM1ByUXIuwdhUYf6QlwwSTaf/KfUycfyHmdq6o8naig2I3jcvqMsBI\n1748K4RVaeLP2vtNWZPLDe3P6qn90n/ECdmqWNtP/63FMBb5PfXuGrkTXl2lj+pY\no9gdBe3WmmJ+EW4iOn5/4nQQEYlVOpg3OmimoZaeEXp5PYopPRI4y34lihO6Bbuo\nkKlWkM3aWForx7M20GUsy+Q8OqZ/RTdnjYoa7bRdtG1BXntP7rA/Nrw2Up50PxJJ\nMF7MGcXhhOH7GSjHCB6/3jXbRfo6iCKdqtx0rPm2mJNa/DBpNfcRAILlZT0jGFeS\nnQzLmXpKOtpe7S080w2yFm/aUfcUdJW0C1Ly3aCY0i5/5zbXBho2at+Gerrh+r01\nq28BhVLmiOq9IoGl4dDtwmt7kcLJ7BWie5USa30q10cYiwUMjjSMKBP+9idNzBjn\n6REl/Lmn9XEAM1R9fxvrEua9d6pU768IoatjN/Bn39QstD0HTe/GJ7I7mGEiRota\nWAg/spK5n7EYpgTHdZB2\n=66W2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T19:00:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"