-09-20T20:33:15Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v0.0.7\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) The central credentials (`system.credentials.*`) are available in the scripts as `SECRETS`, the same way the javascript adapter exposes them: `SECRETS.CameraPassword.key`. Editing a credential in the admin UI reaches the running scripts immediately. Can be switched off per instance.\n* (@GermanBluefox) The editor offers the stored credentials after `SECRETS.` and that credential''s fields after the next dot. The API stub describes `SECRETS` as well, so PyCharm, IntelliJ IDEA and VS Code complete it for scripts edited outside the tab.\n* (@GermanBluefox) Requires Python SDK 0.11.0, which brings the decryption of the stored credentials with it instead of leaving it to an optional extra. py-controller rebuilds the environment once.","tree":{"sha":"ce8f182f223634c4b0f859ed78bcf1d5d7daee65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/ce8f182f223634c4b0f859ed78bcf1d5d7daee65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/6ba4a0fe1e85e8e2567e7a722760f6b05dd886e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin