d":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/3ef767fec7adc3f6eddd69b3b4c1c5e177571296","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDNlZjc2N2ZlYzdhZGMzZjZlZGRkNjliM2I0YzFjNWUxNzc1NzEyOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13","sha":"1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13"}],"sha":"3ef767fec7adc3f6eddd69b3b4c1c5e177571296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3ef767fec7adc3f6eddd69b3b4c1c5e177571296"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:34:35Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T21:34:35Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: print becomes a log line, and a script body that blocks costs only its thread\n\n`print()` in a logic script reached the log only because the controller\ncaptures the process''s stdout, and what arrived there had no time, no\nlevel, no instance and no script -- the log pane glued it under whatever\nrecord came before. It goes through the script''s log now, like\n`log.info`, typed in scripting.pyi and documented in both languages.\n\nThe script body no longer runs on the event loop. It is user code, and\nthe shape a user reaches for first is a loop of its own --\n`while True: ... time.sleep(5)` at module level. On the loop that single\nscript froze the whole adapter: no heartbeat, so admin showed the\ninstance yellow; no pump, so `sigKill` went unanswered and every stop\nended with the controller killing the process; and nothing anywhere said\nwhy. It runs in a worker thread now. A body that has not returned after\n`blockedWarnSeconds` is named in a warning, the other scripts start\nmeanwhile, and its triggers are registered whenever it does return.\n\nBecause the body runs off the loop, `set_state`, `get_state` and\n`send_to` hand their coroutine to the loop with\n`run_coroutine_threadsafe` when they are called from there.\n\nA watchdog thread reports a loop that has stopped ticking -- a handler\nstill runs on it -- and reports when it comes back. The previous one\nmeasured dispatch duration from the loop it was watching, so in the one\ncase worth reporting it was as stuck as everything else.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b74eb0ae31df0dc1e3b50f69fddd140d96ff377f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/b74eb0ae31df0dc1e3b50f69fddd140d96ff377f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDFlOTFkYzAxMWE1NzY0YzA0YjA3NGNmZGY2NWFkYWNjMTI3NmVjMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3","sha":"0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3"}],"sha":"1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/1e91dc011a5764c04b074cfdf65adacc1276ec13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:22:01Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:22:01Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v0.0.3\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016xQMrkCWhkjKm3tpXbZZ4T","tree":{"sha":"dd11ea2563f63e51b76b8cb7f7ff18c2a182b80e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/dd11ea2563f63e51b76b8cb7f7ff18c2a182b80e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDA5MDJhNWE3MWEyODg2NDljMTljNzZmNDk5ZDQ5MzYyYjViZjM0ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f","sha":"405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f"}],"sha":"0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/0902a5a71a288649c19c76f499d49362b5bf34f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:58:55Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:58:55Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"ci: run the adapter''s Python tests, instead of calling them an integration test\n\n`test:integration` is the script the ioBroker adapter action runs\nunconditionally, and here it was `pytest -q`. On a runner with no Python\npackages installed that is `sh: 1: pytest: not found`, on every leg of a nine-way\nmatrix, for tests that were never going to run there.\n\nThey deserve better than that name. The script engine, the selectors and the\nscheduler are what this adapter *is*, and their tests talk to a real Redis\nbecause what they exercise is behaviour against a database rather than a mock of\none. So they get a job: Python 3.10 and 3.13, Redis installed and waited for,\n`ruff check`, `pytest -q`. 84 tests that had never run in CI now do, and deploy\nwaits for them.\n\nThe adapter action is told there is no harness-based integration test, which is\nthe truth and will stay it for a while: starting this adapter needs a built\nvirtual environment, and the harness has no way to provide one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015McHmTR6q5oWNfBsvtkcui","tree":{"sha":"9a209d14df211b0f14798e06b9979e56cc2ee5b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/9a209d14df211b0f14798e06b9979e56cc2ee5b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDQwNTc4MTc4MWM3YWE2NjUxZGZlZjQ3ZWVlZDQ4MjEyNjMzNzAwN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/1e050b01631d04fc133fc2567e79d9e99d1de65d","sha":"1e050b01631d04fc133fc2567e79d9e99d1de65d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/1e050b01631d04fc133fc2567e79d9e99d1de65d"}],"sha":"405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/405781781c7aa6651dfef47eeed482126337007f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/1e050b01631d04fc133fc2567e79d9e99d1de65d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:49:31Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T17:49:31Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: declare the node types src-admin uses, instead of borrowing them\n\n`vite.config.ts` imports `node:url` and types a request as `IncomingMessage`,\nand `@types/node` was in nobody''s dependencies. It type-checked here anyway,\nbecause TypeScript walks up the directory tree looking for `node_modules/@types`\nand this working copy sits inside an ioBroker installation that has them --\nC:\\pWork\\node_modules\\@types\\node, two levels up. A CI runner has no such\nparent, so the same command failed there with \"Cannot find name ''node:url''\".\n\nDeclared in src-admin now, where it is used, and named in the `types` array so\nthe dependency is visible rather than implied. Pinned to the major the borrowed\ncopy was, so nothing about the local build changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015McHmTR6q5oWNfBsvtkcui","tree":{"sha":"c3abbba5b6465175da70d507a98c5e45113d0686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/c3abbba5b6465175da70d507a98c5e45113d0686"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/1e050b01631d04fc133fc2567e79d9e99d1de65d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u