,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/54e686c9309e1572e8d43e05bc47b495fd70539d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/7bb68e24c4e0772d7bae3dc65d6c90dbb78bfba2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/7bb68e24c4e0772d7bae3dc65d6c90dbb78bfba2","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDdiYjY4ZTI0YzRlMDc3MmQ3YmFlM2RjNjVkNmM5MGRiYjc4YmZiYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75","sha":"fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75"}],"sha":"7bb68e24c4e0772d7bae3dc65d6c90dbb78bfba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/7bb68e24c4e0772d7bae3dc65d6c90dbb78bfba2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T15:57:23Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T15:57:23Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: script tabs, a help dialog, completions -- and a traceback that stays with its error\n\nCommitted as one because it cannot be taken apart any more: the editor work\nthat arrived through the day and my changes to the log pipeline are woven\nthrough the same files. What is in here:\n\nThe editor grew tabs, so several scripts are open at once, with the source\nkept per tab and unsaved work surviving a switch. A documentation dialog\nrenders the reference from `assets/doc`, and the editor offers completions\nfrom a typed stub of the script API. Monaco replaced the plain textarea,\nwhich is what pulls in the worker and the icon font.\n\nThe log pane learnt to filter. Every line the engine writes now carries the\nfull script id -- `[script.py.Test.my_script1]`, not `[my_script1]`, because\ntwo scripts in different folders share a name but never a path -- and the\npane turns that into a field it can filter on. The default follows whatever\nthe editor has open, so moving between scripts brings the right log along,\nwhile an explicit choice survives the switch. Trimming is per source, so a\nchatty script can no longer push a quiet one out of the buffer entirely and\nleave its pane looking empty.\n\nThe last piece is why a traceback used to go missing. The host forwards the\nprocess''s stdout line by line, one socket message per line, so only the first\nline of a record carries the header that says which script raised and at what\nlevel. Every frame after it became its own unattributed info line -- filed\nunder \"Engine\", and invisible the moment the pane showed one script, which is\nexactly when a traceback is wanted. A headerless line now joins the entry\nabove it and inherits its script and severity. Verified against the real\nmessage shape rather than a reconstruction of it: six messages, one entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"5c510e500a8dd514f41de08cb3d65805874a7591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/5c510e500a8dd514f41de08cb3d65805874a7591"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGZjMmNiZTdlMjRiNjBjNDBjOGQwYjQzMzE5N2M4ZTI2MDU1M2NiNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755","sha":"b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755"}],"sha":"fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/fc2cbe7e24b60c40c8d0b433197c8e260553cb75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:16:04Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:16:04Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: conditions are snake_case only, and say so when they are not\n\nReverts accepting `valGt` beside `val_gt`. This is Python, and an API that\nanswers to two spellings teaches neither -- the cost is not the substitution,\nit is a codebase where both appear and neither is the rule.\n\ncamelCase stays recognised for one purpose: naming the right spelling.\n`valGt=80` is refused when the script loads, with \"did you mean ''val_gt''?\".\nThat is a refusal, not a second spelling -- nothing runs until it is written\nthe python way -- and it saves the round trip through the log that a bare\n\"unknown condition\" would cost someone arriving from the javascript adapter.\n\nA name that resolves to no field either way, like `valGrt`, gets no\nsuggestion: inventing one would send the reader somewhere else that is also\nwrong.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"b79144ef3a6c09b3adebfbaa26e6877286bdb0aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/b79144ef3a6c09b3adebfbaa26e6877286bdb0aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGIxZGY1NmMyNDNiODMwZDBmZDgzZjEwNDUzMDg5MjViMDJlMGU3NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851","sha":"a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851"}],"sha":"b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/b1df56c243b830d0fd83f1045308925b02e0e755"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:05:36Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T11:05:36Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: accept the javascript spelling of a condition, and declare userPackages\n\n`valGt=80` now means `val_gt=80`, `oldVal` means `old_val`, `channelName`\nmeans `channel_name`. Refusing camelCase was the wrong call: it is what\nsomeone porting a script has in their fingers, and translating costs one\nsubstitution while refusing costs them a round trip through the log.\n\nThe reason for refusing it still holds and still applies -- a name that\nresolves to no field at all is rejected when the script loads, so `valGrt`\ndoes not quietly become a trigger that fires on everything. Only the ones that\ndo resolve are translated. The error names the condition as it was written,\nnot as it was normalised: being told `val_grt` is unknown after typing\n`valGrt` sends the reader looking in the wrong place.\n\nAlso declares `native.userPackages`, the list py-controller reads to install a\nuser''s own Python packages into this adapter''s environment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"e4f9b1e18d9da172503711c2830e1c5cc8963213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/e4f9b1e18d9da172503711c2830e1c5cc8963213"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGExN2YwMTdhZDMzY2NkYzc0MTc4ZDM1MzBiNDFlNmIyYThkYWQ4NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef","sha":"48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef"}],"sha":"a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a17f017ad33ccdc74178d3530b41e6b2a8dad851"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:45:33Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:45:33Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: trigger conditions on on(), as keyword arguments\n\nThe javascript adapter''s `on()` takes a pattern object with 49 selectors.\nCounted, they are not 49 ideas: `val` and `oldVal` crossed with six\ncomparisons, `ts`/`oldTs`/`lc`/`oldLc` with five, `from`/`oldFrom` with two,\nplus ack, q, six tree selectors and `change`. They exist in that shape\nlargely because Blockly and the rules editor generate them; someone typing a\nscript there usually writes an `if`.\n\nSo the same surface, derived instead of enumerated:\n\n    @on(\"hue.0.lamp.level\", val_gt=80, ack=True)\n    @on(\"hue.0.lamp.level\", change=\"ne\")\n    @on(\"sensor.0.*.motion\", enum_name=\"Living room\")\n\nA name reads as `field` or `field_operator`, split at the last underscore and\nonly when the tail is an operator -- so `old_val` stays one field and\n`old_val_gt` becomes one. Equality means \"matches\", as it does there: a list\nmatches any entry, a compiled regex matches by search, and an enum field --\nwhose value is a list -- matches by membership.\n\n`valGt=80` is refused when the script loads, naming the fields. That is the\nmistake someone arriving from JavaScript will actually make, and a condition\nsilently dropped leaves a trigger firing on everything with nothing to\nexplain why. An unorderable comparison decides False rather than raising: a\ntrigger that cannot decide has not fired, and one bad comparison must not\ntake the dispatch loop with it.\n\nThe id may now also be a list or a compiled regex. A regex says what to\naccept but not what to ask for, so it widens the subscription to everything\n-- documented, because that cost is invisible otherwise.\n\n`logic: ''or''` is deliberately absent: two triggers, or an `if`, say it more\nplainly than a flag that changes what the other keys mean. And none of this\nis required -- every condition stays equally sayable as an `if`, because the\nhandler receives the event that carries all of it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"6a0632b85743cf2bd155eed80f584e666ca75c46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/6a0632b85743cf2bd155eed80f584e666ca75c46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDQ4ZmU1MGUxYzdlMjI1MzVlMDBhNzFkZWE0YTNiYWZhY2JmYWExZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f","sha":"9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f"}],"sha":"48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/48fe50e1c7e22535e00a71dea4a3bafacbfaa1ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:33:02Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:33:02Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat!: a handler takes the event, and only the event\n\nThe two- and three-parameter shapes are gone. They were carried as\ncompatibility with a contract that never existed outside this repository --\nthe adapter is a day old -- and they were not free: they cost a signature\ninspection per registration, a three-way branch on the hottest path in the\nsystem, and a stored arity per handler.\n\nThey also did damage. A handler declared `(id, state)` gets the value and\nnothing else: no previous state, no name, no channel, no enums. That shape is\nwhat led a script here to reach for `state.oldVal` -- an attribute that\nexists in neither engine -- because the event that does carry the old state\nhad been unpacked away before the handler could see it. Offering less as a\nconvenience is not a convenience.\n\nA wrong signature is now refused when the script loads, naming the handler\nand saying what a handler takes, instead of raising the same TypeError on\nevery state change for as long as the script runs. The rest of the script\nkeeps working: one bad trigger costs its own trigger, not the file.\n`inspect.signature().bind()` decides it, so *args and defaults are judged by\nwhether the call would actually work rather than by counting parameters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"e2e990cc282c4b42f208e5a585260abb995d1255","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/e2e990cc282c4b42f208e5a585260abb995d1255"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDllZDZlOTk0Njk3YmFkZmM0ZTA5NmVmZDA1MWI2MjUwN2EzZDFjNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af","sha":"83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af"}],"sha":"9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/9ed6e994697badfc4e096efd051b62507a3d1c4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:20:46Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:20:46Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: tag every log line with the full id of the script it belongs to\n\nThe tag was the script''s name, so `[my_script1]` -- and a name is not an\nidentity. Two scripts in different folders are called the same thing all the\ntime, and their lines landed in one indistinguishable pile. It is now\n`[script.py.Test.my_script1]`: the full object id, the one thing that is\nunique, which is what lets the log pane offer a filter at all.\n\nLines the engine writes *about* a script carry it too -- started, stopped,\ncould not be started, and the engineType refusal. Those are the ones a user\ngoes looking for when a script is not doing anything, and they were exactly\nthe ones that named no script in a machine-readable way.\n\nBracketed and leading, so the pane can strip it with an anchored match rather\nthan hunting the text for something id-shaped: a line that merely mentions a\nscript -- an error quoting one -- must not be filed under it. What the engine\nitself says stays untagged, which is what makes \"engine only\" a filter of its\nown rather than a leftover.\n\nAlso drops the \"older spellings\" framing around the two- and three-parameter\nhandlers. There is nothing older here: the adapter is hours old and nothing\nwas ever written against a previous contract. They are alternatives that\nunpack the event, and that is all they are.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"7b6d777103d619fc6a19b3a8f995314924e299d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/7b6d777103d619fc6a19b3a8f995314924e299d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDgzYzQ3ZTQ4MzM2MDI4ZTNkZDllMTllN2VjMjcxOTQ0OTIwNDkwYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337","sha":"918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337"}],"sha":"83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/83c47e48336028e3dd9e19e7ec271944920490af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:09:59Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:09:59Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"docs: correct the trigger semantics and fill in the API details\n\nFollow-up to 0cb1fd8, whose message described a draft that a concurrent edit\nhad already replaced -- the commit carries that message over different\ncontent, and over eight i18n files it should never have touched. My mistake:\ncommitting without a pathspec swept in an index someone else was filling.\nThis one is limited to the file it talks about.\n\nThe correction that matters is the trigger. The text said `on` runs \"whenever\na matching state changes\"; it runs on every write that reaches it, including\none writing the same value again -- Script.dispatch compares no values. The\njavascript adapter''s `on(''id'', cb)` is short for `change: ''ne''`, so a ported\nscript fires more often here than it did there, silently. Now stated, with\nthe two-line comparison that restores the old behaviour.\n\nAlso: `expire` is gone from the state attributes. It exists on the dataclass\nbut neither from_wire nor to_wire carries it, so on an event it is always\nNone -- documenting it would have sent people looking for a value that never\narrives.\n\nAdded what the page was missing for its actual audience: what each state\nattribute means, a javascript-to-python name mapping, and the mistakes that\ncost real time -- `state.oldVal`, which exists in neither engine and crashed\na script here today; a forgotten `await`; and `time.sleep()`, which stops\nevery other script in the instance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"d77f79f6f478ead39cbeb41e4e877e3146d3810e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/d77f79f6f478ead39cbeb41e4e877e3146d3810e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDkxOGE5MmYyMDVmOThlOTA0MTZhZDZhOWQ3NTgyMjFjZjI1N2EzMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9","sha":"0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9"}],"sha":"918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/918a92f205f98e90416ad6a9d758221cf257a337"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:02:02Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:02:02Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"docs: reference for the scripting engine''s methods and objects\n\nWritten against the code rather than from memory, and checked back against it:\nevery name the text promises is really in the namespace a script sees, every\npattern and cron expression in the tables was parsed by the real parser, and\nall 18 examples compile.\n\nTwo things it says that are easy to get wrong. `on()` here fires on every\nwrite, while `on(''id'', cb)` in the javascript adapter is short for\n`change: ''ne''` and fires only when the value changed -- someone porting a\nscript gets duplicate work otherwise. And `state.oldVal` does not exist,\nin neither engine: in JavaScript `oldVal` is a pattern selector deciding when\nto fire, not a property of the state. The previous value is\n`event.old_state.val`, which is None for the first change after a start.\n\nNothing loads this file yet; wiring it into the editor is a separate change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"c2d07f941a06f15cf23870964e84a97c33accb6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/c2d07f941a06f15cf23870964e84a97c33accb6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDBjYjFmZDhjZTQ0ZDc4OGQxMjE1MDE1YTFiYjhhOTQyNDhhMmNjZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989","sha":"78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989"}],"sha":"0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/0cb1fd8ce44d788d1215015a1bb8a94248a2cce9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:17:15Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:17:15Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: require iobroker>=0.6.0, the version the engine actually needs\n\nThe engine calls get_object_list(), terminate() and reads the exit-code\ncontract -- none of which exist in the SDK 0.5.0 the manifest declared.\npy-controller dutifully built an environment that satisfied that\ndeclaration, and the adapter then died on startup with\n\n    AttributeError: ''ScriptHost'' object has no attribute ''get_object_list''\n\nand restarted in a loop. Raising the floor makes the environment hash\nchange, so an existing installation rebuilds instead of staying broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"664bd2f428d8e956e2e15a52bc1e480e37aa11b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/664bd2f428d8e956e2e15a52bc1e480e37aa11b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDc4YjcyMDUyY2VkYTExZWY1YTMwYTNiOTliNWE3YThjMDEyMDI5ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c","sha":"c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c"}],"sha":"78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/78b72052ceda11ef5a30a3b99b5a7a8c01202989"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:30:27Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:30:27Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: serve the tab at the dev server root\n\n`npm start` showed a blank page at localhost:3000. The entry is tab.html, because\nthat is the name admin loads from /adapter/python/, but vite''s dev server answers\n`/` with index.html and nothing else -- so the tab was only reachable at\n/tab.html, which is not something anyone should have to know.\n\nA dev-only middleware rewrites `/` to `/tab.html`. Renaming the entry to\nindex.html would have worked too, but then the build would have to rename the\noutput back, and the file would no longer be named after what it is.\n\nVerified against a running dev server: GET / now answers 200 with the tab.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"0c2dd34c5facfbad103df8238d3ec46ad2acc9c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/0c2dd34c5facfbad103df8238d3ec46ad2acc9c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGMxZTY5ZWVhNWVmYTA5Mzc4MGI1N2IzZTFmYzZjODAxNGE5NzA0N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf","sha":"a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf"}],"sha":"c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/c1e69eea5efa093780b57b3e1fc6c8014a97047c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:12:15Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:12:15Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: put the log controls in a vertical strip, as the javascript adapter does\n\nThe controls sat in a horizontal bar above the log. That works below the editor\nand wastes the width the log needs when the pane sits beside it, which is the\nlayout the new switch makes possible.\n\nThey now live in a 34 px column down the left, the width and arrangement\nioBroker.javascript uses, with a shadow separating it from the lines and the\ntitle beside it rather than above. Copy and Clear appear only while there is\nsomething to copy or clear -- the same condition the original puts on them,\nwhich is why an empty log shows three buttons and not five.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"54398a7aad5ce4480dbba622e08a25e870ae9e5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/54398a7aad5ce4480dbba622e08a25e870ae9e5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGExNzEyYzc0NmYwMzlhOTE2MzVkMWI3YzEyYTVhNGFhZDkxM2QyY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c","sha":"e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c"}],"sha":"a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a1712c746f039a91635d1b7c12a5a4aad913d2cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:06:08Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:06:08Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: handlers receive an event object, like the javascript adapter''s EventObj\n\nThe handler contract was (id, state) -- the adapter-level shape, not the script\none. In the javascript adapter an `on()` callback receives a single object\ncarrying the whole context of the change, and that is what someone writing\nioBroker scripts expects. This closes that gap.\n\n`Event` mirrors src/lib/eventObj.ts field for field, adapted to Python: id,\nstate (an alias of new_state, as there), old_state, common, native, name,\nchannel_id, channel_name, device_id, device_name, enum_ids, enum_names.\n\nTwo properties of the original were worth reproducing exactly. Everything past\nthe two states is lazy and then remembered -- functools.cached_property is what\n`doGetter` does by hand with Object.defineProperty -- so a handler reading\nevent.state.val and nothing else pays for nothing else. And enum membership is\ninherited from the parent object: a state in a channel that is in a room counts\nas being in that room, which is what makes `event.enum_names` useful at all.\n\nAnswering synchronously means holding the object tree in the process: loaded once\nat startup and kept current by subscribing to every object change, exactly as the\njavascript adapter does. That is the price of `event.channel_name` being an\nattribute rather than something to await, and it is the same price ioBroker\nalready pays on the JavaScript side.\n\n(id, state) and (id, state, old) are still dispatched -- scripts written against\nthem are running in installations right now -- but the event is the contract, and\neverything beyond the bare value is only reachable through it.\n\ntest_event.py covers the object itself and needs no database, so this part of the\nengine is testable without Redis: translation of names, the inheritance rule, the\nmemo being given up when an enum changes, and that nothing resolves until read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"bfdabb5c2bac310bfe64d66f290fc2b19f25f952","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/bfdabb5c2bac310bfe64d66f290fc2b19f25f952"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGU0NmJkNDQzNjQzZWQyYWY5NGVjZjNjN2Y3MzIzYTdjY2MxMGM5M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e","sha":"d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e"}],"sha":"e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/e46bd443643ed2af94ecf3c7f7323a7ccc10c93c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:59:01Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:59:01Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: log pane controls -- follow, layout, hide, copy, clear\n\nThe pane had a Clear button and followed the tail only while the user happened\nto be scrolled to the bottom. It now carries the same controls as the javascript\nadapter''s log, and for the same reasons.\n\nFollowing the newest entry is an explicit switch rather than something inferred\nfrom the scroll position: reading an older line no longer silently turns it off,\nand turning it back on is one click instead of a scroll to the bottom.\n\nThe pane can sit beside the editor instead of below it. The splitter is\ndeliberately remounted on the change: it reads initialSizes once, and the same\npercentages mean widths in one direction and heights in the other.\n\nHiding leaves a small handle in the bottom right corner, the way the javascript\nadapter brings its log back -- without it, hiding the log is a one-way door. All\nthree switches are remembered in localStorage, next to the pane sizes.\n\nCopy puts the whole buffer on the clipboard with ISO timestamps and severities,\nwhich is the form that is useful in a forum post.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"be8e1a14150693e863146509d500d4edca4a9e29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/be8e1a14150693e863146509d500d4edca4a9e29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGQwYmFjYjE0MzFlYzBjZmIzZDBiZTg1OTQ5OTk1MzA0MWQ5MDgwMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19","sha":"103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19"}],"sha":"d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/d0bacb1431ec0cfb3d0be859499953041d90802e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:51:34Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:51:34Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: hand handlers the previous state, and fix the icons in the state picker\n\nTwo things a first real script run turned up.\n\nA script reaching for the value before the change got\n`AttributeError: ''State'' object has no attribute ''oldVal''`. That is a genuine\ngap, not a user error: in the javascript adapter an `on()` handler receives\n`obj.state` *and* `obj.oldState`, so anyone coming from there will reach for it.\n\nA handler declared with a third parameter now receives the previous state, or\nNone for the first change after the engine starts. Opt-in through the signature,\ndecided once at registration rather than per event: two-parameter handlers are\ndispatched exactly as before, so nothing existing changes and the feature costs\nnothing to scripts that do not want it.\n\nIt is remembered by the engine, not the SDK -- the same division ioBroker makes,\nwhere adapter-core reports a change and the script engine is what remembers what\ncame before. Putting it in the SDK would have given every Python adapter a cache\nit never asked for.\n\nSecond, every adapter icon in the state picker rendered as a broken image. The\ndialog resolves icon paths relative to the page, and this tab lives under\n/adapter/python/ rather than admin''s root. imagePrefix=\"../..\" is what the\njavascript adapter passes for the same reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018RTbquksLNHLZ8x6nLrHxC","tree":{"sha":"5ccc1a8dbbcd638f3e850d271cb0b017fbb64325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/5ccc1a8dbbcd638f3e850d271cb0b017fbb64325"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDEwM2I1OGMyNGUyZWIyNzI3N2NiMTc4ZDE3ZjRmY2MxYWY4M2FiMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53","sha":"df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53"}],"sha":"103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/103b58c24e2eb27277cb178d17f4fcc1af83ab19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T05:50:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T05:50:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"test: give the adapter suite its own Redis database, and leave it empty\n\nBoth this suite and the SDK''s own (ioBroker/iobroker-python) defaulted to Redis\ndatabase 15, and this one only flushed on setup. So running the adapter tests\nleft `python.0` keys behind, and the SDK suite -- which refuses to flush a\ndatabase holding keys it did not write -- then declined to run at all: 110 errors\nbefore a single test.\n\nTwo changes, because either alone leaves a hole. The default is database 14, so\nthe two suites no longer share one; and the fixture now flushes on teardown as\nwell as setup, so it leaves the database as it found it whatever database it is\npointed at.\n\nVerified by running both suites back to back: 31 passing here, then 286 passing\nin the SDK, where the second run previously could not start.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SMZrkEWcycb2RhAtd58S4v","tree":{"sha":"88a1a73d23e95d22bc6b712927b8591269fad8aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/88a1a73d23e95d22bc6b712927b8591269fad8aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGRmODE5ODg3YjIyY2YwZTNmYmY4YzM5ZjRiYTliYzA0Y2Y3ZmNhNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449","sha":"065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449"}],"sha":"df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/df819887b22cf0e3fbf8c39f4ba9bc04cf7fca53"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T05:21:17Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T05:21:17Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"build: move the Python package manifest to where py-controller looks for it\n\npy-controller builds an environment by running `uv pip install .` with the\nadapter''s `python/` directory as the working directory, and hashes\n`python/pyproject.toml` to notice dependency changes. This adapter kept its\nmanifest in the repository root, so the build would have run in a directory\nwithout one and failed.\n\nThe manifest now sits in python/, next to the module, and declares a build\nbackend -- without one the install falls back to setuptools'' legacy\nauto-discovery, which is not something a package should leave to chance.\n\nThe root pyproject keeps only tool configuration (pytest, ruff), whose paths are\nrelative to it and which are run from the repository root. Splitting them is what\nlets both live where they belong.\n\nVerified by building the wheel: all five modules are in it and the metadata\ncarries `Requires-Dist: iobroker>=0.5.0`, which resolves -- the SDK is published\non PyPI as `iobroker`, currently 0.5.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SMZrkEWcycb2RhAtd58S4v","tree":{"sha":"b594005aef65b6fdcf8751b6e9d94cdb8e780dea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/b594005aef65b6fdcf8751b6e9d94cdb8e780dea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDA2NWExODllNzUyZTNhNTljYTY5YTFhODE1ZjVjMzM0NDcyNGU0NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e","sha":"9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e"}],"sha":"065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/065a189e752e3a59ca69a1a815f5c3344724e449"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:53:21Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:53:21Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"test: validate the package metadata\n\n`npm run test:package` runs @iobroker/testing''s package validation. That matters\nmore here than for an ordinary adapter: this one declares common.platform\n\"Python\" and a main pointing into python/, fields almost nothing else uses, so a\nmistake in them surfaces only when the controller refuses to start an instance.\n\nIt found one straight away: package.json had no `main` at all. A Python adapter\nhas no Node entry point -- the controller starts python/<module>/__main__.py from\nio-package.json -- but the validator requires the field for every non-onlyWWW\nadapter, so it is named there now and the package describes its own entry point.\nThat check does not know about Python adapters yet; the field is the workaround,\nnot the fix.\n\nNo @iobroker/testing integration test, and there cannot be one yet: that harness\nempties the data directory before every test, and a Python adapter''s virtual\nenvironment lives inside it. Without an environment js-controller refuses to\nstart the instance, so the harness''s mandatory \"The adapter starts\" test waits\nfor an `alive` that never arrives. The runtime is covered by the pytest suite,\nwhich starts a real host against a real database. Reason recorded in the README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"9c6b28f1a1718fa63af7d0935b9c683d0f8f134a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/9c6b28f1a1718fa63af7d0935b9c683d0f8f134a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDkyOTJhODA5YjdjNTYxNzdhZDlhY2ZjZjAyNDA4Nzg2OGE0MTU0N2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a","sha":"cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a"}],"sha":"9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/9292a809b7c56177ad9acfcf024087868a41547e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:33:09Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:33:09Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: validate the name while typing, and move scripts by drag and drop\n\nUniqueness was only checked after the dialog closed, as an error toast. It is now\nchecked on every keystroke: the Create button stays disabled and the field shows\nthe reason. Both namespaces are checked rather than just the one being created --\na script and a folder are both objects and cannot share an id, so a script named\nlike an existing folder collides too.\n\nWhile the name is valid the helper text shows the id the item will get. That\nmakes two things visible before anything exists: which folder it lands in, and\nwhat the sanitising did to any characters ioBroker does not allow.\n\nDrag and drop moves a script between folders. Dropping on a folder row moves it\nin; dropping anywhere else in the tree moves it back to the top level, which is\nthe way out again. ioBroker has no rename, so a move writes the object under the\nnew id and deletes the old one -- create first on purpose: if the delete then\nfails the script exists twice, which a user can fix, while the other order could\nlose it. The open script follows its new id before the delete, so the delete''s\necho is not mistaken for \"the script being edited disappeared\". A folder''s drop\nhandler stops propagation, otherwise the root drop zone behind the tree would\nalso fire and the script would land at the top level instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"275f189778c119505164c33668316747bc46fe19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/275f189778c119505164c33668316747bc46fe19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGNkNGEyYzM2YzIzZjYwNjk0OTc5M2U0ODhkYTJjMzk5ZGUwNDNkMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80","sha":"a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80"}],"sha":"cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/cd4a2c36c23f606949793e488da2c399de043d0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:30:06Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:30:06Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: Save/Cancel stayed up after the edits were undone\n\n`changed` was a flag set on the first keystroke and cleared only by saving,\ncancelling or switching script. Typing something and then removing it again --\nby hand or with undo -- left the flag set, so Save and Cancel kept offering to\nsave a file identical to the stored one.\n\nIt is now derived: the editor content compared with the stored source. That is\ntrue by construction for every route back to the original, including undo, and\nit removes seven places that had to remember to reset the flag.\n\nTwo knock-on effects worth having: switching script no longer asks \"discard the\nunsaved changes?\" when there are none, and the run controls (which show while\n!changed) come back as soon as the edit is undone. Saving now also updates the\nstored copy in local state, because the derived value compares against it and\nwaiting for the subscription echo would leave the buttons on screen for a moment\nafter a successful save.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"12c691f7cbc591020d8d63bb6e366720d009f435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/12c691f7cbc591020d8d63bb6e366720d009f435"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGE4YTNjM2JkY2MwNjBhZWUyNzIxYjE1ZDE0NWUzYTE3NjUyNmJlODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b","sha":"69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b"}],"sha":"a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/a8a3c3bdcc060aee2721b15d145e3a176526be80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:21:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:21:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: start/stop in the toolbar, and a way into an empty folder\n\nThe editor toolbar was missing the third of the three controls\nioBroker.javascript has. Now: Locate (expands the folders above the script and\nscrolls the row into view, rather than only expanding), Restart, and Start/Stop.\n\nFollowing the original, the run controls appear only while there is nothing to\nsave -- the mirror of the Save/Cancel rule. Restarting a script whose editor\ncontent differs from what is stored would run the old source and look like a bug.\n\nThe tab now follows `<instance>.alive`, which lets the toolbar name the reason\ninstead of leaving a coloured dot to be interpreted: \"Script is not running\" when\nit is disabled, \"Instance is disabled\" when the engine itself is down, and\n\"Enabled, but the engine did not start it\" for the case only this adapter can\ndetect -- a script that failed to compile. Restart is hidden while the engine is\ndown, since it could not do anything.\n\nCreating a script inside a folder was impossible: the target folder was derived\nfrom the selected script, and folders could not be selected, so an empty folder\nwas unreachable. A folder is now also a create target -- one click opens it and\npicks it -- and every folder row has a \"New script in this folder\" button, which\nis the discoverable way. Selecting a script clears the pick again, so \"New\"\nfollows what you are looking at. Dotted names still create the folders they name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"929b39015740e5f7df21d6840ab8675d9d38d433","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/929b39015740e5f7df21d6840ab8675d9d38d433"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDY5ZWE5NDA0Yzk4NTc1Mzk4ZWM2M2I0ZTA5OTQ4NGYxMTIzNTIxN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2","sha":"dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2"}],"sha":"69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/69ea9404c98575398ec63b4e099484f11235217b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:17:41Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:17:41Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: Enter in the name dialog reopened it immediately\n\nEnter was handled in onKeyDown, which closed the dialog while the key was still\ndown. MUI then restored focus to the toolbar button that had opened it, and the\nnext auto-repeat of the same keystroke pressed that button -- so a second dialog\nappeared the instant the first one was confirmed.\n\nTwo changes, one per mechanism. The dialog body is now a real form: Enter\ntriggers exactly one submit and preventDefault stops the browser acting on the\nkeystroke a second time, with the action button as type=\"submit\" and Cancel\nexplicitly type=\"button\" so implicit submission can never reach it. And both\ndialogs set disableRestoreFocus, so closing does not hand focus back to the\nbutton that opened them -- which is what turned a key repeat into a reopen. The\ndelete dialog had the same latent problem through its autofocused Cancel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"e6b28d5ed4caa323775ad9bd1dba0daeecd91a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/e6b28d5ed4caa323775ad9bd1dba0daeecd91a0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGRlZGUyOGFiYTUyOWFjOTNmNjg0YTI0MDIwYWQ5MjlkMTQ4ZDVjZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593","sha":"77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593"}],"sha":"dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/dede28aba529ac93f684a24020ad929d148d5cd2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:59:16Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:59:16Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: official Python logo, draggable panes, and ioBroker dialog conventions\n\nLogo: admin/python.png is the official mark, downloaded unaltered from\npython.org. The PSF policy allows exactly this use -- non-commercial, nominative,\nand it names icons for files and executables explicitly -- but only while the\nshape is unchanged, so the file ships byte-for-byte rather than redrawn. The\nofficial SVG was the first choice and was rejected: it carries no viewBox and its\npath coordinates run negative, so it would not scale without me inventing a\nviewBox I cannot verify here. Attribution and the commercial-use caveat are in\nthe README.\n\nPanes: the sidebar and the log pane are now on draggable splitters using\n@devbookhq/splitter, the same library ioBroker.javascript uses, with the sizes\nremembered in localStorage and a corrupt entry falling back to the default rather\nthan keeping the tab from opening.\n\nSave/Cancel are rendered only while something has changed. Their appearing is\nitself the unsaved-changes signal, which beats a permanently present pair of\ngreyed-out buttons.\n\nDialog buttons now follow the ioBroker order, taken from gui-components'' own\nDialogConfirm rather than guessed: the action first, Cancel always rightmost,\nboth contained, with Check and Close icons and Cancel in the grey palette.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"2c2e40836c8a1123af04cc25299ae18f8cf82c10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/2c2e40836c8a1123af04cc25299ae18f8cf82c10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDc3NTAwMjk0ZTIzMjk4ODEyMDBjYmNjMTA4M2EyNDJmYTFkM2Q1OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84","sha":"3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84"}],"sha":"77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/77500294e2329881200cbcc1083a242fa1d3d593"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:43:50Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:43:50Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: shape the tab like the javascript adapter''s script editor\n\nRead what ioBroker.javascript''s buttons actually do and rebuilt the equivalents\nrather than guessing. From SideMenu.tsx: the row''s play/pause toggles\ncommon.enabled, the trash deletes, the third icon is \"Edit script or just double\nclick\". From Editor.tsx: Locate file, Save, Cancel, Undo/Redo, and the group on\nthe right -- <> is \"Prettify the script\", the clock is the CRON wizard, the wand\nis AI Chat, the clipboard is \"Insert object ID\".\n\nPorted: the folder tree, per-row start/stop/delete/edit, Locate, Save, Cancel,\nUndo/Redo, Insert object ID, CRON, Restart. Left out with reason: Prettify (no\nformatter ships in the adapter''s venv), Debug and AI Chat (no equivalent here),\nBlockly/Rules (JavaScript-only).\n\nFolders are real `channel` objects the way the javascript adapter stores them, so\nan empty folder exists and survives a reload instead of being inferred from\ndotted ids. The tree merges both sources -- folder objects and folders implied by\na script id -- so a script cannot vanish because its folder object is missing,\nand a folder is only deletable while empty.\n\nOne deliberate improvement over the original: there the play/pause icon can only\nreflect `enabled`. Here the button still toggles `enabled`, but the colour\nreports what the engine really does -- green when running, amber when enabled but\nnot running, which is the state a script with a syntax error is in and which the\njavascript adapter cannot show.\n\nAlso: undo/redo keeps its own history (a controlled textarea has no native undo),\ncoalescing bursts of typing into one step; a search filter that keeps the folder\npath to each match; expand/collapse all; and a prebuild step, because the bundle\nname changes every build and emptyOutDir is off, so stale bundles were piling up\nin admin/assets.\n\nVerified: strict type-check and build clean, and buildTree exercised at runtime\nfor implied folders, empty folders, nested counts, ordering and filtering.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"ed089c6badb1e45251f664be73df29cd1fae758a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/ed089c6badb1e45251f664be73df29cd1fae758a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDNlYjUyNzA2ZmIwZmU4MTJiNjZlYzRiNGU0YzMyN2IzMDA3NDdkODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6","sha":"ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6"}],"sha":"3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3eb52706fb0fe812b66ec4b4e4c327b300747d84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:36:18Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:36:18Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: keep text files at LF\n\nA helper script run on Windows rewrote README.md to CRLF, turning a twenty-line\nedit into a two-hundred-line diff. Restored, and .gitattributes now pins LF so it\ncannot happen again; built bundles under admin/assets are marked generated so\nthey stay out of diffs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"9f3ef1b0636258f1331f41b04574e37d3d5eb90c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/9f3ef1b0636258f1331f41b04574e37d3d5eb90c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGZmMDQ2MjliNjkzNmNhOWRhNWQ1ZmVmYjExYjAwYjEwYjg3MDE2YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246","sha":"dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246"}],"sha":"ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/ff04629b6936ca9da5d5fefb11b00b10b87016b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:35:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:35:05Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"docs: record the py-controller prerequisite\n\njs-controller only ever checks whether a Python environment exists -- it never\nbuilds one. Without the py-controller adapter on the same host there is no\nvirtual environment, so an instance of this adapter never starts.\n\nNot declared in io-package.json yet, deliberately: iobroker.py-controller is not\npublished, and depending on a package that does not exist would make this\nadapter impossible to add. Until then the prerequisite shows up as an instance\nthat never starts rather than as a refused installation, which is worth saying\nout loud -- so it is in Requirements and tracked in \"What is missing\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"b2c5f75d90f597d2e6ca25546f56ba2b74cd3b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/b2c5f75d90f597d2e6ca25546f56ba2b74cd3b25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKGRkM2U5Mzg4MWFlNzJlNzg2MzE5YzdjODAwZDMzNDdkYjI4YTUyNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd","sha":"092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd"}],"sha":"dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/dd3e93881ae72e786319c7c800d3347db28a5246"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:11:16Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T12:11:16Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: rebuild the admin tab as a React app on the admin stack\n\nReplaces the hand-written HTML tab with a React app in src-admin/, on the same\nstack ioBroker.javascript uses: React 19, MUI 9, @iobroker/gui-components and\nVite, building into admin/.\n\nThe two components that make the editor more than a text box come straight from\ngui-components, and both insert at the caret rather than just handing back a\nvalue: DialogSelectID puts the chosen state id in as a quoted string, which is\nwhat @on(...) needs, and DialogCron inserts a whole @schedule(\"...\") decorator\ntrimmed to the five fields the engine''s cron parser accepts.\n\nApp extends GenericApp with AdminConnection, bottomButtons: false (a tab manages\nobjects, it does not edit this instance''s config) and autoSubscribeLog, which is\nwhat feeds the log pane through registerLogHandler. Script changes arrive live\nvia subscribeObject; an edit made elsewhere is followed unless there are unsaved\nchanges here.\n\nThe code editor stays a highlighted <pre> under a transparent <textarea> rather\nthan Monaco: Monaco would have to be bundled or fetched and an ioBroker box is\noften offline. The invariant that technique needs -- rendered text with tags\nstripped equals the source, or the overlay drifts from the caret -- was verified\nagainst a sample covering comments, all three string forms, decorators, keywords\nand numbers.\n\nOne ~1.5 MB chunk by design: React/MUI/gui-components are bundled instead of\nshared with admin through module federation. A self-contained bundle in an\niframe always works; federation is an optimisation that cannot be verified\nwithout a running admin. Splitting the dialogs out would not help -- they come\nfrom the same package as GenericApp.\n\nVerified: strict type-check passes, the build is clean, io-package.json still\nvalidates against js-controller''s schema, and the Python suite is unaffected\n(31 passing). Still not opened in a live admin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"641703248ed2d22acebeffa0a56160e4106d28b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/641703248ed2d22acebeffa0a56160e4106d28b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDA5MmY5ODgwNzdlMWU2NmY1NDExZjU1ZjQyMmM2YzdiZDBjMzk5YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a","sha":"3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a"}],"sha":"092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/092f988077e1e66f5411f55f422c6c7bd0c399bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T11:38:49Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T11:38:49Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: admin UI -- instance settings and a script editor tab\n\nDeclared the way ioBroker.javascript declares its own, which was worth checking\nrather than guessing: adminUI {config: json, tab: html} plus adminTab\n{singleton, name}, with the tab at admin/tab.html.\n\nadmin/jsonConfig.json gives the instance two settings, and both do something --\nblockedWarnSeconds now drives the host''s watchdog instead of the hardcoded 2s,\nand maxLogLines bounds the tab''s log pane. A settings page whose settings are\ndecorative is worse than none, so the wiring has tests.\n\nadmin/tab.html is a single self-contained file with no build step: script list,\nPython syntax highlighting, enable/disable, new/delete, a Reload button that goes\nthrough the adapter''s own messagebox commands, and a live log pane filtered to\nthe selected instance. The javascript adapter''s tab is a React/Vite app with\nmodule federation; for a prototype a file you can edit and reload beats a\ntoolchain, and the <pre>-under-<textarea> highlighter means nothing is fetched\nfrom a CDN -- it works on an offline Raspberry Pi.\n\nThe tab could not be opened in a running admin here, and the README says so. What\nwas verified: io-package.json validates against js-controller''s schema, the\ninline JavaScript passes node --check, and the highlighter provably preserves its\ninput exactly (rendered text with tags stripped is identical to the source) and\nescapes correctly. The connection follows @iobroker/socket-client, shows its\nstate in the header, and falls back to /socket.io so a failure is visible rather\nthan silent.\n\nAlso: ruff reads a logic script''s injected names (on, set_state, log, ...) as\nundefined, which users linting their own scripts will hit too -- scoped to the\nexamples here, documented for script authors in the README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"54e5a15df4b0fc471c9c2425c18e9a7d926a1cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/54e5a15df4b0fc471c9c2425c18e9a7d926a1cd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a","node_id":"C_kwDOUN-dLNoAKDNjMzZhMTk1MDVmYjhiZWJiOGVlMGQ0OTI2OTg4N2VlM2Y1MWZlM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commit/5bd88ce05d9cc9878c67d20585b5247975ae9ce1","sha":"5bd88ce05d9cc9878c67d20585b5247975ae9ce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/5bd88ce05d9cc9878c67d20585b5247975ae9ce1"}],"sha":"3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/3c36a19505fb8bebb8ee0d49269887ee3f51fe3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/commits/5bd88ce05d9cc9878c67d20585b5247975ae9ce1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:33:12Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:33:12Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"feat: prototype of the Python logic-script engine\n\nioBroker.python is to Python what ioBroker.javascript is to JavaScript: it runs\nuser logic scripts. Scripts are ordinary ioBroker `script` objects routed by\n`common.engine`, the field several javascript.N instances already use to share\none script tree -- so this engine and the javascript adapter coexist in\n`script.*` without stepping on each other, and the existing editor can manage\nPython scripts without knowing anything about Python.\n\nThe adapter is itself a Python adapter (common.platform: \"Python\"), started\nnatively by js-controller and talking to the databases through the Python SDK.\nThat is the point of the design: nothing bridges between Node.js and Python at\nruntime. Bolting Python onto the javascript adapter would have meant that Node\nprocess spawning Python children, supervising them and tunnelling the whole\nscript API over IPC -- rebuilding what js-controller already does.\n\nThe script API mirrors the javascript adapter''s, because its users already know\nthat one: on(), schedule(), set_state(), get_state(), send_to(), log, on_stop().\nHandlers may be def or async def -- writes return a task, so a plain def handler\nfires and forgets while an async def one can await the same call; reads must be\nawaited. Cron is a ~50 line five-field parser rather than a dependency.\n\nAll scripts share one process as asyncio tasks: a process per script would cost\n30-50 MB and its own pair of database connections each. A blocking script stalls\nits neighbours, exactly as a while(true) stalls the javascript adapter today, but\nthe host names the culprit; compile errors and raising handlers are contained.\n\nCovered by 28 tests against a real database, including the routing rules, live\nreload on edit, and containment of broken scripts. Verified end to end over the\nreal controller start path (python -u -m iobpython with IOB_* in the\nenvironment), down to a clean exit 0 on sigKill -1.\n\nNo admin UI yet -- see README \"What is missing\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RHRA5jcXoxKrSWs69kq5g","tree":{"sha":"f77bc7fd7a5d8eb3e154074688f348755d769e09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/trees/f77bc7fd7a5d8eb3e154074688f348755d769e09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.python/git/commits/5bd88ce05d9cc9878c67d20585b5247975ae9ce1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/G