da/MetalCalc/commits/0343e45f5c5a32b0e7f0c3ef9b2f91ecb6010d5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:04:04Z","email":"rabdeepsinghkharbanda29@gmail.com","name":"Rabdeepsingh-Beaconstac"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:04:04Z","email":"rabdeepsinghkharbanda29@gmail.com","name":"Rabdeepsingh-Beaconstac"},"message":"Add keyword research data, FAQPage/ItemList schema, metadata on all content\n\n- Committed .claude/brain/seo/keywords.json (21 Google Autocomplete seeds,\n  210 raw long-tail suggestions) + keyword-map.md (page -> primary keyword\n  -> long-tails -> intent) driving this and future content work.\n- New src/utils/faqJsonLd.js: shared FAQPage JSON-LD builder, used by\n  Faq.jsx (refactored), BlogPost.jsx and LandingPage.jsx.\n- Seo.jsx: jsonLd prop now accepts an array (multiple schema blocks per\n  page) in addition to a single object, backward-compatible, with cleanup\n  of stale per-page script tags on navigation.\n- All 15 blog posts + 10 landing pages now carry category (Metals/Markets/\n  Tools), keywords[], updated date, and a faqs[] array (5 Q&As each,\n  grounded in the keyword data) — FAQs render visibly on-page (required\n  for FAQPage rich results) and feed the new schema.\n- BlogPost.jsx: BlogPosting JSON-LD extended with image/keywords/wordCount/\n  dateModified, plus FAQPage. LandingPage.jsx: new Article + FAQPage\n  JSON-LD (previously had no page-specific schema at all).\n- Blog.jsx: posts now grouped by category, plus an ItemList JSON-LD.\n- Brain docs (029/030) updated with the new object shape and keyword-data\n  pointer for future content additions.\n\nThis is the schema/metadata layer of the content-depth pass approved in\nplan mode. Full prose expansion (1,200-1,600 words/post, beginner-friendly\nper explicit feedback) is the next batch — posts are currently ~250-450\nwords each, below target; this commit doesn''t change that yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha"