m/users/WorkRabdeepSinghKharbanda/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WorkRabdeepSinghKharbanda","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WorkRabdeepSinghKharbanda/MetalCalc/commits/e07bef103f1c13a5a8802390c2722702e81d4211/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T23:54:21Z","email":"rabdeepsinghkharbanda29@gmail.com","name":"Rabdeepsingh-Beaconstac"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T23:54:21Z","email":"rabdeepsinghkharbanda29@gmail.com","name":"Rabdeepsingh-Beaconstac"},"message":"Add 10 blog posts and 10 SEO landing pages\n\n- 10 new blog posts (position sizing, RSI, melt vs retail, FX margins, tax\n  reverse-calc, diversification score math, correlation vs diversification,\n  storage/insurance carrying cost, alloy mixing math, 52-week range proxy) —\n  appended to src/blog/posts.js, same BlogPosting JSON-LD pattern as before.\n- 10 new static landing pages via a single generic dynamic route\n  (/:landingSlug -> LandingPage.jsx, data in src/content/landingPages.js).\n  React Router ranks static routes above it automatically, so it can''t\n  shadow any existing page. Adding a page going forward: append to\n  landingPages.js + sitemap + llms.txt, no new route/component needed.\n- All registered in appRoutes (command palette), sitemap.xml, llms.txt, and\n  the brain index (029/030 cover the blog and guides mechanisms — one entry\n  each, not one per post/page, since brain-sync.md tracks routes/mechanisms\n  not individual content items).","tree":{"sha":"bf3dba9d01c9fee0a63fe1605dddf785d23c468b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WorkRabdeepSinghKharbanda/MetalCalc/git/trees/bf3dba9d01c9fee0a63fe1605dddf785d23c468b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WorkRabdeepSinghKharbanda/MetalCalc/git/commits/e07bef103f1c13a5a8802390c2722702e81d4211","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avata