thub.com/users/dev-araujo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dev-araujo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dev-araujo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dev-araujo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dev-araujo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dev-araujo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-araujo/crypto-tracker-mfe/commits/3507c7199d5d5769ff4f4662e7633bd271490611/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:13:58Z","email":"theriancirculo@protonmail.com","name":"araujo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:13:58Z","email":"theriancirculo@protonmail.com","name":"araujo"},"message":"feat(api): proxy Coinranking through the server so the key stays private\n\nThe credential was compiled into the client bundle, so publishing the\nsite published the key with it. The client now always calls\n/api/coinranking on its own origin and never sees a token: a Vercel Edge\nFunction injects it in production, and the Angular dev-server proxy does\nthe same locally, so both environments exercise the same code path.\n\nThe proxy is not an open relay - it accepts GET and HEAD on the three\npaths the application actually uses. Responses carry s-maxage=60, so the\nCDN serves one upstream call to every visitor within the window instead\nof one per person, which cuts quota consumption further than the\nin-memory cache alone could.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0151zPR5ShEZdi4rY5CAPkGn","tree":{"sha":"c877272cc10ac9de0c1609534cd85dad08ec045f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-araujo/crypto-tracker-mfe/git/trees/c877272cc10ac9de0c1609534cd85dad08ec045f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-araujo/crypto-tracker-mfe/git/commits/3507c7199d5d5769ff4f4662e7633bd271490611","verification":{"payload":nu