mit/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","sha":"3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419","sha":"31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419"}],"sha":"4a07694f8c01ac45a35713dfd7e9fddaff662b81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/4a07694f8c01ac45a35713dfd7e9fddaff662b81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:28:33Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:28:33Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Call the beta.4 host contract from the MCP tools\n\nThe tools dispatch to window.CyWebApi by string, so nothing type-checked\nthe six places where the host''s development branch had moved on: four\nrenames (additiveUnselect → additiveDeselect, setColumnName →\nrenameColumn, removeMapping → deleteMapping, getNetworkList →\ngetNetworks) that failed with METHOD_NOT_FOUND, and two signature changes\nthat failed inside the host — the selection calls now take\n(networkId, nodeIds, edgeIds) and createContinuousMapping takes an\noptions object instead of six positionals. The three selection tools''\ninput schemas split `ids` into `nodeIds` and `edgeIds` to match, the way\ncytoscape_select already did; passing a mixed list as nodeIds would have\nsilently dropped every edge.\n\nThe return-shape changes (getAvailableLayouts, getNodePositions) are left\nalone: those tools pass the host''s data through untouched.\n\nThe panel''s api-types pin moves to ^1.0.0-beta.4, now that it is\npublished; the panel itself uses none of the changed APIs and type-checks\nunchanged. MCP_TOOLS.md and the Phase 1 checklist reflect the six repairs.\n\nVerified against a local host on development: every dispatch string\nresolves in the beta.4 declarations, and each repaired tool round-trips —\nselection add/toggle/remove with split ids, rename_column, and a\ncontinuous mapping created then deleted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce47d775c7b4bf0c0b0a73327418f33a1b8543f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/ce47d775c7b4bf0c0b0a73327418f33a1b8543f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDMxNTIyZDg1MTdmYWUwMDJiMjMxMjQzZDA1ZDcyOGMzYjMwM2I0MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","sha":"3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf"}],"sha":"31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/31522d8517fae002b231243d05d728c3b303b419"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T01:06:06Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T01:06:06Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Add the WebMCP roadmap, and fix two defects it exposed\n\nThe roadmap evaluates an externally drafted WebMCP plan against the code and\nagainst the WebMCP spec, Chrome''s documentation and the Chrome DevTools MCP\nreference as they stood today. It sits above the workflow plan: the plan holds\nunit contracts, the roadmap holds order, dependencies and release conditions.\n\nIts central claim is that the seven broken tools exist because tool definitions\nlive in the wrong repository. Once the host owns the operation definitions, that\nclass of bug is gone by construction — for every consumer, whether or not WebMCP\never ships. WebMCP is a beneficiary of host-owned operations, not the reason to\nhave them.\n\nTwo defects in the existing plan were found while reviewing it, and both would\nhave survived into the implementation:\n\n- Verification counted non-default values, so an analysis whose correct answer\n  is zero everywhere would have failed. Pass/fail is now decided per id —\n  value, type and missing-ness — with counts as diagnostics.\n- The apply operation built the result network from the analysis-input\n  snapshot, which for a 400k-node dataset imports 400k nodes into the browser:\n  exactly what the projection exists to prevent. It now works from four named\n  references and imports only the projection.\n\nDecisions recorded, with reasoning in the revision lists:\n\n- Browser support is Chromium-based. Firefox removed CDP in 141 and Safari\n  isolates automation sessions by design; the one route serving both would have\n  cost a WebSocket connector, pairing, and a permanent certificate burden, and\n  delayed the first releasable result. Three cheap things keep the door open —\n  a Transport interface, an informational Firefox/WebKit job, and honest\n  wording. The connector survives as a proposal, motivated by the WSL2 setup.\n- Completion is four states, not one. The host''s persistence scheduler defers\n  writes 300 ms and logs failures, so an API success proves the store changed,\n  never that it was saved.\n- WebMCP registration is tiered: read and view-only mutations now, data\n  mutations only behind a host-enforced write contract, destructive operations\n  never.\n- The initial release applies analysis as a new network only. In-place apply\n  moves to the proposals.\n\nAlso: a guide README, since four documents now need one, and it names the gap\nit found — P1a and P1b have no checklist sections yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"66ada6aefa549218d235c3b5eeaba258b46eb087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/66ada6aefa549218d235c3b5eeaba258b46eb087"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDNmNzA5MmVhNTI1NGVlYWI3MmIwMzM4OTMzM2E1ZGIyODkxNzY2Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef","sha":"4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef"}],"sha":"3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/3f7092ea5254eeab72b03389333a5db2891766cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:03:05Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:03:05Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Run CI on development, now that it is the default branch\n\nThe workflow triggered on `main` only, so moving the default left every push\nunchecked — the design-document commit went in with no CI run at all. Both\nlong-lived branches are listed now: `development` is where the work happens,\n`main` is the snapshot the repository was split at.\n\nThe concurrency guard had the same `main`-only assumption, and would have\ncancelled superseded runs on `development` instead of letting each pushed\ncommit keep a full result.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b8cb047cb54a51c3a4a762bc56f63f6f1ee0d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/5b8cb047cb54a51c3a4a762bc56f63f6f1ee0d58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDRhNThiMDI2OTVhMzVlOTdlZDViODI2MDc0ODJmZTcwNDNmNzJjZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b","sha":"e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b"}],"sha":"4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/4a58b02695a35e97ed5b82607482fe7043f72cef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:57:53Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T08:57:53Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Plan the agent workflow: design, checklist, open proposals\n\nDesign documents for turning the bridge from a demo into a tool an analyst can\nrely on, and from a Claude-specific tool into one any MCP client drives.\nNothing is implemented; this is the plan and its audit.\n\nThe audit is the part worth reading. Seven tools cannot work against the host''s\ncurrent App API, and only three of those are visible to a method-name check —\n`createContinuousMapping` and two selection tools kept their names and changed\ntheir signatures. Ingest passes data through the model''s context while\nretrieval already writes files. CX2 does not round-trip through the App API in\neither direction: import drops opaque aspects and visual style options, and\nexport drops style options and every opaque aspect after the first key. The\nTSV join needs an id map, because CX2 edge `7` is `e7` inside the host, and a\nnew numeric column is created with `0` for every element, so a missing value\nand a real zero are indistinguishable.\n\nSix review rounds shaped this, and the corrections are recorded in the\nrevision list rather than quietly folded in: the release branch turned out to\ncarry no App API at all, `Function.length` is not a contract, `get_table`\nalready summarises, an all-unmatched import still creates columns, and the\n`window.CyWebApi` presence check does exist — as a guard on an already-chosen\npage rather than a way to choose one.\n\nThree files:\n- agent-workflow.md — the plan, §1-§14, with what was measured and why\n- agent-workflow-checklist.md — four phases, each with tests and verification\n- agent-workflow-proposals.md — nine open proposals, finding separated from\n  proposal so the two can be judged apart\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9620beba66406ce138b2e3e7c6be2b90ddb1e3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/a9620beba66406ce138b2e3e7c6be2b90ddb1e3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKGU3YjA0M2U2NmMwNWU2MmE2ZmNmZWRjNDIwNDY0NTc0M2Y4NTEyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f","sha":"8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f"}],"sha":"e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/e7b043e66c05e62a6fcfedc4204645743f85122b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:50:12Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:50:12Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Format mcp-server with the repository''s Prettier config\n\nThe 12 files under mcp-server/src/ had never been through Prettier: in the\nexamples repository they sat in a workspace nobody formatted, and .prettierrc\nwas a root file the app half honoured and this half did not. src/ was already\nclean, so the split is what made the inconsistency visible in one tree.\n\nWhitespace only — `tsc` produces the same output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a07e49e7a4c7c0cd922c4aba5f731af52d2106e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/a07e49e7a4c7c0cd922c4aba5f731af52d2106e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDhmODVlMTg2ZDBhNzA5YzBiNjMwMjZlMzI5NTg2MWRmY2FhNzJjNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11","sha":"cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11"}],"sha":"8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/8f85e186d0a709c0b63026e3295861dfcaa72c5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:20:43Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:20:43Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Stand on its own: repository scaffolding after the split\n\nExtracted from cytoscape-web-app-examples with its history, where this was the\nclaude-bridge/ workspace. What the workspace root used to supply now has to\nlive here: .nvmrc, .prettierrc.json, .gitignore, .gitattributes, LICENSE, a\nlockfile, and CI.\n\n- The app builds, typechecks and tests unchanged — its package.json already\n  declared every dependency it uses, which is what made a copy-out possible.\n- Paths in prose and comments rewritten for the new root: claude-bridge/src/ →\n  src/, design/apps/claude-bridge/ → design/.\n- CI covers both halves separately, because they are separately built: the app\n  through Vite, mcp-server through plain tsc with its own lockfile. The app job\n  asserts the built federation container still matches package.json''s cyweb.id.\n- .eslintrc.json was NOT carried over: the source repository declared no eslint\n  dependency and no lint script, so it configured a linter that never ran.\n\nThe federation id (claudeBridge), the dev port (6100) and both package names\nare deliberately unchanged, so the host''s app registry and existing .mcp.json\nentries keep working. Renaming is a separate decision from moving.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1d4ac45705628a5e4e6006c898f63aeb847d194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/e1d4ac45705628a5e4e6006c898f63aeb847d194"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKGNkMzUyMTY2NDQ4YTBkZGQwNjJiZWEwOGI5NDBmNWUwZGU3MDFmMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84","sha":"f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84"}],"sha":"cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/cd352166448a0ddd062bea08b940f5e0de701f11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:17:21Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T01:17:21Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Add ''design/'' from commit ''330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c''\n\ngit-subtree-dir: design\ngit-subtree-mainline: ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda\ngit-subtree-split: 330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c","tree":{"sha":"301a4851a126008a7bf3422f6ab76dde7c2be3de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/301a4851a126008a7bf3422f6ab76dde7c2be3de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKGYwNDFhNWZkZTZlYzdjNWM0OWUxZTMyY2EwODI3MDIzNDM0YTNlODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda","sha":"ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c","sha":"330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c"}],"sha":"f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/f041a5fde6ec7c5c49e1e32ca0827023434a3e84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:24:50Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T23:24:50Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"0.4.0-next.1: the submission manifest, as a Developer Preview\n\nBoth packages move to 0.4.0-next.1 in lockstep, and so does everything that\nnames them. The five examples had to move too: `^0.3.0` does not admit a\nprerelease, so npm would have gone looking for 0.4.0-next.1 on a registry that\ndoes not have it yet rather than linking the workspace copy.\n\nGenerated projects pin the preview EXACTLY. A caret over a prerelease admits\nonly prereleases of the same major.minor.patch — neither the stability an exact\npin gives nor the breadth a caret suggests — and the SDK_VERSION test picks\nwhich rule applies from whether the runtime''s own version is a prerelease, so\nthe pin and the runtime cannot drift apart in either direction.\n\nThe schema and predicate identities stay under /draft/, and no document claims\nformatVersion 1 is stable. Issuing the stable identity freezes the envelope, and\nthat waits on the handshake in issue #8.\n\nOne test was depending on suite order. The byte-identity check between the CLI\nand the packager read whichever archive happened to be lying around, so it\nstarted failing the moment the version bumped: a stale archive carries the\ngenerator string of whatever SDK built it. It now builds its own archive from a\nfixture both suites share.\n\nPrepared, not published. Publishing runs from the release workflow after this\nmerges, so the artifact and its provenance attest to a commit on the main line\nrather than to a feature branch. Rehearsed locally: 49 files, 65.8 kB, the\ntemplates present in the scaffolder tarball, and the repository field the\nregistry validates and a dry run never sees.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23bef1c26decac64c8bad6710789382ce241a425","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/23bef1c26decac64c8bad6710789382ce241a425"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKGFiOTI5OWVmNzkxMzIzMmVlZGQ3NGM1ODYxYWEyZTk0NTQxN2NmZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2","sha":"cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2"}],"sha":"ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/ab9299ef7913232eedd74c5861aa2e945417cfda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:44:05Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:44:05Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Ship the manifest to generated projects, the examples, and CI\n\nEverything the packager can do was only reachable from this monorepo, where\nadm-zip arrives transitively through the Federation plugin and `build:zip`\ntherefore works by accident. Generated projects now declare it themselves,\nbecause a project relying on that would break the day that plugin stopped\nneeding it. The five maintained examples gain the script and both of its\ndependencies — none of them declared `cross-env` either, and the repository root\ndoes not provide it, so adding only the script would have shipped a documented\ncommand that does not run. All five now build an archive: 18, 10, 18, 16 and 14\nmembers, each with one root manifest and one root entry and no HTML, source map\nor Federation metadata.\n\nThe scaffolder gained the half of the version rule that is not a refusal. A\nversion outside the submission profile — build metadata, over-length, a numeric\nidentifier past MAX_SAFE_INTEGER — is legal SemVer and builds and runs fine; the\nrule is about a ZIP filename and a URL path segment. So it warns on stderr,\nexits 0, and writes the project, and `build:zip` is where it actually fails. All\nthree halves are verified end to end. `cy-manifest.json` joins the generated\n.gitignore, since a copy committed beside the package.json it is derived from is\na second source of truth nothing keeps in step.\n\nCI stops testing the wrong thing. The scaffold job installed the REGISTRY copy\nof app-runtime whenever the generated range already resolved, using the\ncandidate tarball only as a fallback — so an ordinary SDK change could pass a\npre-publish gate while exercising code published weeks ago. It now always\ninstalls the candidate, asserts the resolved package sits inside the generated\nproject, and asserts `cyweb-app --version` matches it. It runs under npm AND\npnpm, which the SDK design already made an acceptance criterion but which only\nnpm had ever satisfied, and under pnpm it asserts the runtime plugin resolves\ninside the installed package — a path escaping it fails silently at load time.\nEach template now also builds an archive and reads the manifest back out.\n\nA windows-latest job covers what no amount of Linux testing reveals: rename over\nan existing file, separators in member names, and the order they come out in.\nThe packager turns adm-zip''s locale-dependent sorting off and uses one named\ncomparator precisely so the answer is the same on both, which is only worth\nclaiming if it is executed somewhere.\n\nPost-publish smoke follows the workflow''s `tag` input rather than a hard-coded\n`next` — the workflow can publish `latest` — asserts the tag actually moved\ninstead of printing it beside the version, then installs through the tag,\nscaffolds, and reads a manifest out of a real archive.\n\nDocs: getting-started §5b said `npm run build` writes the zip, which stopped\nbeing true when the zip became opt-in and stayed on the page for longer than it\nshould have.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d46fab39a9b428899dfd15ffbace1bdfc9f1bffe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/d46fab39a9b428899dfd15ffbace1bdfc9f1bffe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKGNkZTIzNzgzYWFmOTYwZTNkZmUyZWZhNzc1ZDgyOWEwODFmYWRiZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a","sha":"26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a"}],"sha":"cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/cde23783aaf960e3dfe2efa775d829a081fadbe2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:35:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:35:49Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Release 0.3.0: zip as a build option, and a scaffolder that survives a paste\n\nTwo changes reach app developers only through a release, so both go out\ntogether.\n\n`npm run build:zip` makes the App Store archive a per-build decision\nrather than an edit to the one file the SDK tells you not to write.\nCYWEB_APP_ZIP sits underneath it and works in both directions, so an app\nthat commits `appStoreZip: true` can still skip the zip while iterating.\n\nThe scaffolder no longer prompts into a pipe. Pasting the Quick Start''s\nthree-line block fed `cd my-app` and `npm run dev` to the prompts as\nanswers and exited 13 on an unsettled await; a non-TTY stdin now takes\nthe defaults and says so (#6).\n\nVersion, the pin scaffolds emit, all five workspace consumers and the\nlock move together, because they have to: `^0.2.0` does not admit\n0.3.0, and leaving a consumer behind makes npm resolve app-runtime from\nthe REGISTRY while the repository appears to test the new code. That was\nthe 0.2.0 lesson and the guards for it -- the SDK_VERSION test and\n`npm ci` -- both pass here.\n\nTarballs check out: app-runtime 31 files, create-cytoscape-app 58 with\ndist/interactive.js present.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc2a731fef8c6bb8b084d5525fa8010209a1f261","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/fc2a731fef8c6bb8b084d5525fa8010209a1f261"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDI2Y2YwMzlhYWE5OWEzMzFkNGQwZDZjZWMzN2MyNzc5ODU1OTU2NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c","sha":"2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c"}],"sha":"26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/26cf039aaa99a331d4d0d6cec37c27798559564a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:14:29Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T21:14:29Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Carry the 0.2.0 bump into the workspace consumers and the lock file\n\nThe release rehearsal failed at `npm ci`: package-lock.json still\nrecorded app-runtime 0.1.0. Bumping a workspace package''s version is not\na local edit -- every consumer''s range has to move with it, and the lock\nhas to be regenerated, or the tree no longer describes itself.\n\nWorse than a stale lock, and the reason this needed care rather than a\nquick `npm install`: all five example apps declared `^0.1.0`, which a\n0.2.0 workspace no longer satisfies. Regenerating the lock without\ntouching them made npm resolve app-runtime from the REGISTRY instead of\nthe workspace -- so the repository would have built and verified against\nthe published 0.1.0 while appearing to test the new code. The ranges are\nnow ^0.2.0, matching SDK_VERSION, and the lock links the workspace again\n(zero registry entries for app-runtime).\n\nThe lock diff is seven lines, all of them this bump. Nothing else was\nallowed to drift in.\n\nProcess note: this class of failure was already guarded. ci.yml runs\n`npm ci` in five jobs -- but only on push to main/development or on a\nPR, so a feature branch does not trigger it, and dispatching the release\nworkflow straight from the branch reached npm ci with no earlier warning\nand burned an environment approval. Merging before releasing is what\nputs the guard back in front.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b7d0116091dcf0e69aef279e9307698aedc900b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/0b7d0116091dcf0e69aef279e9307698aedc900b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDJmYTE0MzcxYzUyZDAyZGM0YmNjYmI0OGU5MjhlOTc1MTk3YzVlM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069","sha":"0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069"}],"sha":"2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/2fa14371c52d02dc4bccbb48e928e975197c5e3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T05:26:37Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T05:26:37Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"App SDK Phase 3: identity through the virtual module, and dev install by link\n\nTwo things that were pre-existing defects rather than missing features.\n\nApp code no longer imports package.json. Every app chunk used to carry the WHOLE\nfile — devDependencies, scripts, the prose comment blocks — because the config\nneeded one string from it. Reading the four fields from virtual:cyweb-app-meta\ninstead removes 6,608 bytes across the five apps, and grepping the built output\nfor \"typescript\" or \"vitest\" now finds nothing.\n\nhello-world had a SECOND importer, HelloHeader.tsx, which the first pass missed:\nthe app config was converted and the bundle was still dirty. Worth recording\nbecause what caught it was grepping the built artifact, not re-reading the\nsource. A source-level check would have reported success.\n\nRegistering an app no longer means editing a file in a repository you do not\nown. `npm run dev` prints a link:\n\n  http://localhost:5500/?installApp=http://localhost:5555/cyweb-app.json\n\nThe dev server answers /cyweb-app.json from the parsed package.json on every\nrequest. Deliberately not a tracked public/cyweb-app.json, which the design\npredicted would break the build and does: public/ is copied into dist/, where\nthe App Store publish allowlist matches no rule for it and fails on purpose.\nGenerating it per request also means changing cyweb.port or the version cannot\nleave a stale copy behind. The host has accepted ?installApp= all along; nothing\nneeded building there, only pointing at.\n\nDescriptions move into package.json. They lived in the CyApp object, richer than\nthe npm-style one-liners sitting beside them; package.json is now the single\nsource and carries the user-facing text, which is also what the install manifest\nserves to the host.\n\nVerified against a stock host, not asserted: the dialog reads \"Install into this\nworkspace?\" and names the app from the served manifest, and Install produces\nInstalled app \"template\" (activate=true) -> App template mounted -> App\n\"template\" activated. Opening the right-side panel to look at the rendered\ncomponent was NOT automated and is left unticked in the checklist rather than\nclaimed — that is host UI navigation, unchanged here, and the right-panel\nresource is already asserted programmatically in Phase 2.\n\nOne scope extension, taken deliberately. The root README was updated as well as\nthe two documents this phase names. It described the flow this phase replaced —\ncopy the template, edit apps.local.json, change DEV_SERVER_PORT — on the\nrepository''s front page. Leaving the first thing a developer reads contradicting\nwhat they would then do is worse than keeping the scope clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"333e50fa6b0b2d4372551c9b6c599afd42618eb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/333e50fa6b0b2d4372551c9b6c599afd42618eb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDBhYTI1MmFhNjQ5ODUyOThmNTJjN2NmZTg1M2IxYWRiMTk4ZTcwNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4","sha":"0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4"}],"sha":"0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0aa252aa64985298f52c7cfe853b1adb198e7069"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T04:39:21Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T04:39:21Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"App SDK Phase 2: migrate the remaining four apps onto the SDK\n\nEvery app now builds through defineCyWebApp. The four copies of\nmfRuntimePlugin.ts, cywebHostSentinel.ts and the runtime-plugin test are gone,\nand each vite.config.ts is three lines. The only deviations the four apps had\nfrom the template were the two constants, hello-world''s second expose and\nnetwork-statistics'' empty share set — which is what the SDK''s options are for,\nand the reason this phase transferred without surprises.\n\nOutput is unchanged where it has to be: all five apps match the Phase 0 baseline\nin every audit field, verify:federation still reports 27/16/26/26/26 with no\nskips, and all five load through the real host loader — hello-world with both\nexposes, network-statistics with none of the React machinery.\n\nfederationName, port and configuredShared are DELETED from apps.manifest.json\nrather than kept and cross-checked. manifest.mjs derives them from each app''s\npackage.json: the first two from the cyweb block the build already reads, and\nconfiguredShared expanded from peerDependencies, which is already the app''s\nstatement of what the host provides. Writing one by hand is now an error that\nnames the field and says to delete the line, because the fix is deletion.\n\nconfiguredShared is derived from peerDependencies rather than from the SDK''s\nCYWEB_SHARED, which is what the checklist asked for. Importing the SDK constant\nwould make manifest:validate depend on the SDK having been built, and CI runs\nthat as a separate job. The check that matters is unaffected and in fact better\nplaced: verify:federation compares the derived records against the BUILT output,\nwhich came from CYWEB_SHARED, so an app disagreeing with the SDK fails there\nwith the artifact as evidence. Observed going red — react ^19.0.0 in one app''s\npeers against an ^18.3.1 build gives \"1 failed, 25 passed\", naming the package.\nvalidatePeerVersions is removed: it compared two hand-written copies, and there\nis now only one.\n\nEach deleted test is replaced by one specific to its app — its identity and the\nshape of what ./AppConfig exports — so no app is left with an empty vitest run,\nwhich would either fail its test script or pass while testing nothing.\n\nOne test is narrower than intended, and the reason is worth recording.\nhello-world''s cannot import NetworkSummaryMenuItem to check its default export:\nthat component calls useWorkspaceApi from cyweb/WorkspaceApi, a federated module\nthat resolves inside the host and not at all under vitest. No component touching\na cyweb/* API can be unit-tested today. That is the gap @cytoscape-web/app-test\nexists to close, and this is direct evidence for it. The expose is covered where\nit can be — verify:federation counts it, which is why this app reports 27 checks\nand the others 26, and the in-host load exercises it for real.\n\nAlso fixes five tsconfig.json comments that still explained a local structural\ntype in src/mfRuntimePlugin.ts, a file that no longer exists in any app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c004d334c5551dc7aa5ef09282a61c4bd02c748e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/c004d334c5551dc7aa5ef09282a61c4bd02c748e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDAzODNiNDRmNjZkZWU3OGY1YTUxYmU5NTVlNmQ4NTljZWY4N2NjZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607","sha":"b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607"}],"sha":"0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0383b44f66dee78f5a51be955e6d859cef87ccf4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T08:26:08Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T08:26:08Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Build an App Store submission zip on every build (cytoscape/cytoscape-web#642)\n\n`npm run build` now leaves `<appId>-<version>.zip` next to each app''s\npackage.json — `template-1.0.0.zip`, `hello-1.0.0.zip` and so on — ready to\nattach to the App Store submission page. Implemented for all five apps as a\nVite plugin in each app''s own vite.config.ts, not a shared script: the template\nhas to keep working as a standalone copy outside the monorepo, which is the\nwhole point of it, and verified below.\n\nThe issue says \"a zipped dist folder\". The zip ships the browser PUBLISH SET\ninstead, which is narrower, because three things in dist/ have no business on a\npublic store:\n\n  mf-manifest.json   embeds absolute build-machine paths — measured, it carries\n                     /home/<user>/… in configuredRuntimePlugins\n  mf-stats.json      6.8 kB of build metadata nothing fetches at runtime\n  SSR entry/loader/  34 kB of Node-only code guarded by\n  module-runner      `typeof window === ''undefined''`, unreachable in a browser\n\nThat is exactly the set copy-dist publishes to GitHub Pages, so the store\nserves what the examples site serves. Verified per app: the zip contents and\ndocs/<app> match file-for-file (16/18/18/10), and the excluded four are absent.\n\nAn allowlist with unmatched-is-fatal, matching copy-dist rather than inverting\nit. An exclusion list would let a future plugin version slip a new file class\ninto a public upload by default, and the mf-manifest path leak is precisely\nwhat that would have missed if the file were ever renamed.\n\nThe zip is written OUTSIDE dist/, which is not cosmetic: a zip inside dist/\nwould be swept into the next one, and copy-dist''s allowlist rejects any file it\ndoes not name — so it would have broken the Pages deploy.\n\nadm-zip, declared in each app rather than leaned on transitively. It was\nalready in the tree via @module-federation/vite, and using it from there would\nrepeat the mistake this migration fixed twice already (@module-federation/runtime,\nterser-webpack-plugin). It has zero dependencies; jszip has four and archiver\nnine, and every app pays for this one.\n\nAPP_ID is now a named constant per app, feeding both `federation({ name })` and\nthe zip name, because the app''s identity has to agree in three places\n(container name, CyApp.id, the host''s apps.json) and a bare literal per use\nsite is how they drift.\n\nVerified: all five build and zip; project-template still installs, typechecks,\ntests and builds — producing its zip — as a clean copy outside the monorepo.\n\nThe docs/ hash churn is a side effect worth naming: the apps inline their whole\npackage.json to read `version`, so adding a devDependency changes the exposed\nchunk. Pre-existing, and the reason the published bundles carry a full\ndevDependencies list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2cb1da2dbcc312df63e5d31e511026ab4f1d2292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/2cb1da2dbcc312df63e5d31e511026ab4f1d2292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKGIzYzNhMmJmMzc0MTkyNWMzNzE1M2RlNGY4MTQ4MzZhZTNjODU2MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760","sha":"9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760"}],"sha":"b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/b3c3a2bf3741925c37153de4f814836ae3c85607"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T23:49:35Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T23:49:35Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Vite migration Phase 7: remove the Webpack toolchain and the docs that assumed it\n\nwebpack, webpack-cli, webpack-dev-server, ts-loader and clean-webpack-plugin\nare gone, verified by deleting node_modules and the lockfile and reinstalling.\nThe root peerDependencies block goes with them: it was the repository''s only\ndirect declaration of @mui/material, react and react-dom, which is why it\ncould not be removed until Phases 4-6 gave every app its own.\n\ncopy-dist loses its `bundler: ''webpack''` exemption — the publish allowlist now\napplies to every app, so an unclassified file is always a failure. The\n`bundler` field and its enum stay: Phase 8 asserts \"every published app is\n''vite''\", and an enum that cannot express the wrong answer cannot catch it.\n\nTwo decisions.\n\ndocs/ was regenerated rather than un-tracked: 32 Webpack outputs (5.8 MB)\nreplaced by the Vite publish set at 1.1 MB, network-workflows alone going\n4.6 MB to 148 KB. That number is section 5.7''s import:false decision showing up\nin the published artifact rather than in a measurement. Keeping docs/ in git\npreserves the property that what is published can be reviewed in a diff.\n\ndocs/index.html''s install instructions were fixed here rather than deferred.\nThey were wrong before this migration and would have stayed wrong: the page\ntells users to paste a remoteEntry.js URL into App Settings, but the host takes\na single-entry MANIFEST url, and appInstallAllowedOrigins is\napps.cytoscape.org / apps-stage.cytoscape.org — cytoscape.org, where the page\nitself is served from, is not on it. Two independent reasons the documented\npath could never work. The page now says so and points at the local dev\nworkflow.\n\nThe \"no webpack references\" exit criterion needed judgement rather than a\nliteral grep. 44 of the 53 remaining mentions in live files explain WHY a\ndecision exists: why type:''module'' is required (the plugin default is a\nWebpack-style global that resolves no exports and fails silently), why the\ntsconfigs set skipLibCheck (the MF SDK''s types `import webpack`), what\n__webpack_public_path__ used to do in HelloHeader. Deleting those deletes the\nreasoning. What was removed is every mention that INSTRUCTS a reader to edit a\nwebpack config or describes this repository as building with Webpack — and\napplying it that way caught two stale instructions the earlier phases missed,\nin HelloApp.tsx and TemplateApp.tsx, both still telling the reader the app id\nhad to match a name in webpack.config.js.\n\ndesign/apps/claude-bridge/CHECKLIST.md and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md keep their\nbuild steps: 92 of 92 items are unticked on an app that has shipped, so they\nrecord a plan rather than instruct anyone.\n\nguides/ gained what the migration made necessary rather than only losing what\nit made wrong: how the host address is resolved at runtime, the symptom of a\nmissing type:''module'' (nothing happens, no error), the symptom of an absent\nhost descriptor, and why hot reload does not cross the federation boundary.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea4f81353c0ed96ef27f1020e45d44765c7de3a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/ea4f81353c0ed96ef27f1020e45d44765c7de3a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDMzMGZhNDhiM2FlMWY4MGM2YWE0MGJmY2JkZTIzMTE1NDAwMDhmN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/0e813f4aaccfd8871c411c814da128f2a4c6c799","sha":"0e813f4aaccfd8871c411c814da128f2a4c6c799","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/0e813f4aaccfd8871c411c814da128f2a4c6c799"}],"sha":"330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/330fa48b3ae1f80c6aa40bfcbde2311540008f7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T22:49:11Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T22:49:11Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Vite migration Phase 6: migrate the remaining three apps\n\nEvery app now builds with Vite. verify:federation and check:imports print no\n`skipped` lines at all — the `bundler` field has finished the job it was added\nfor, and nothing in the repository builds with Webpack any more (the toolchain\nitself goes in Phase 7).\n\nnetwork-statistics is the interesting one. It is the non-React example, and\nthe shape section 7.3 predicted held: no react() plugin, no MUI or Emotion\npeers, configuredShared {}. Its old webpack config declared react, react-dom\nand @mui/material as singletons — the app imports none of them, so that was\none of the pre-existing defects to drop rather than carry across. @types/react\nstays in devDependencies with a comment saying why: the published api-types\ndeclarations reference React types, so removing it looks like a tidy-up and\nbreaks typecheck.\n\nThe verifier reports 16 checks for it against 26–27 for the others. That is\nthe check counts tracking shape, not a regression: with nothing shared, the\nper-package share assertions have nothing to assert. Its smoke observable is\nkind:\"console\" for the same reason — the app renders nothing, so a DOM\nselector would have had nothing to find. Confirmed in a running host against a\nproduction artifact carrying only the sentinel: it mounted and emitted exactly\nits manifest pattern, with no page errors.\n\nnetwork-workflows loses a defect with its config. `mode: ''development''` was\nhardcoded, so `--env production=true` produced a development build; the Vite\nconfig has no such branch and its production build is now genuinely minified\nwith no NODE_ENV branches left in the output. JupyterConnectorPanel''s\nhttp://localhost:8888/lab default is untouched — it is legitimate, and the\nverifier bans only localhost:5500.\n\nclaude-bridge needs no smokeObservable (published: false), and its\nmcp-server/ subpackage is untouched: it is built with plain tsc and\ntsconfig.json''s include already excludes it.\n\nCheck counts, all five green: hello-world 27 (two exposes), network-workflows\n26, project-template 26, claude-bridge 26, network-statistics 16. Twelve unit\ntests per app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9648294833c6ae38b02bcccf179355025ad5923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/f9648294833c6ae38b02bcccf179355025ad5923"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDk5NTZiZmE3N2ZiYzQ3ZTc1MWI5YjhkOTZlMzViNzAyMTBhNDg3NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/19f24a09ec7d298c9d9d6e123967718435f65eb8","sha":"19f24a09ec7d298c9d9d6e123967718435f65eb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/19f24a09ec7d298c9d9d6e123967718435f65eb8"}],"sha":"9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/9956bfa77fbc47e751b9b8d96e35b70210a48760"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commits/19f24a09ec7d298c9d9d6e123967718435f65eb8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:20:42Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:43:18Z","email":"keiono@gmail.com","name":"Keiichiro Ono"},"message":"Vite migration Phase 3: manifest, tooling and CI, with nothing touching an app\n\nScaffolding only. All five apps still build with Webpack at the end of this;\nthe Vite deps are added alongside rather than replacing anything, and every\nnew check is gated on `bundler === ''vite''` so it is inert until an app\nmigrates. tsconfigs are untouched — noEmit would break ts-loader — and the\ntypecheck scripts run against the existing ones.\n\napps.manifest.json is the single inventory. App id, publish path, federation\nname, port, exposes, share block and publish flag were spread across\n`workspaces`, deploy-pages.yml, copy-dist and each bundler config, and two of\nthem already disagreed about which apps get published. `bundler` is what makes\nthe CI scope mechanical: an app joins the Vite-only jobs by flipping one field\nin the commit that migrates it, rather than by someone remembering to edit a\nworkflow.\n\nTwo checks are narrower than the plan said, both because the wider form would\nhave fired where there is nothing to protect:\n\n- The deploy-time host preflight runs only when a published app is ALSO on\n  Vite. A Webpack app compiles the host URL in and never reads\n  window.__CYWEB_HOST__, so a descriptor-less host cannot break it. This is\n  not hypothetical: web.cytoscape.org currently serves runtime.<hash>.js and\n  vendors.<hash>.js — a pre-Vite Webpack build of the host, with no descriptor\n  at all — so an unconditional fatal preflight would have blocked every Pages\n  deploy from this commit onward. Phase 4 arms it by flipping one field.\n- smokeObservable is required on the same condition. The production smoke that\n  reads it selects on published && vite, no app carries a data-testid yet, and\n  four selectors written now would go unexercised until Phase 8.\n\nEach gate was made to fail before being trusted: the manifest loader rejects\nall eight seeded defects (path escape, reserved docs/ asset, duplicate port,\nunknown field, bad enum, duplicate exposes, removed entry, missing\nsmokeObservable); the federation verifier passes 26 checks on a real build and\ncatches a wrong container name, a missing expose and a requiredVersion drift;\npreflight-host has --selftest, which fails if the contract PASSES against a\nhost that publishes no descriptor.\n\ncopy-dist is rewritten around the manifest and fixes two live defects: `cp -r`\ninto an existing directory nested the build as docs/<app>/dist/, and stale\nhashed assets accumulated because nothing deleted first. It now validates\nevery app, stages into a temp directory and swaps.\n\nA probe build of the section 5.5 canonical config settled four things the plan\nhad been assuming — see Rev. 17 for the detail. The most consequential: the\npayload gate cannot be moved out of generateBundle, because a post-hoc scan of\nbuilt files is wrong in BOTH directions. It flags a correct build (the SSR\nloader embeds absolute node_modules paths as dead string literals — section 8\nDecision A, reproduced here) and misses a real one (module paths do not\nsurvive minification). The verifier asserts shared[].assets emptiness instead\nand says in its comments that this is not the section 5.8 gate.\n\nVerified: npm ci clean, all five apps build, typecheck passes for all five,\ncopy-dist reproduces the workflow''s docs/ output. The PR CI workflow and the\npreflight have not run — the first needs a PR, the second a Chromium install\nthis machine lacks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e66fc820a16c3062297957e8af28a7f5d683220","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/trees/3e66fc820a16c3062297957e8af28a7f5d683220"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/git/commits/19f24a09ec7d298c9d9d6e123967718435f65eb8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73890?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/keiono","id":73890,"login":"keiono","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keiono","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/19f24a09ec7d298c9d9d6e123967718435f65eb8","node_id":"C_kwDOUO1Dz9oAKDE5ZjI0YTA5ZWM3ZDI5OGM5ZDlkNmUxMjM5Njc3MTg0MzVmNjVlYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/keiono/cy-agent-bridge/commit/535e25c12d58