tps://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/2e7023bcc4eb2b5e2342200ee9fa8cd326fc0819/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:02:21Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:04:49Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"message":"Say why the list of uploaded archives came back empty\n\nThe catch in loadUploads() clears the list and drops the reason, which\nmakes an instance without uploads look exactly like a read that failed.\nThat cost an afternoon of guessing when the selection appeared empty\nwhile GitHub happened to be rate limiting as well.\n\nThe branch itself stays - without a readable list nothing may be judged\nas missing - it just reports to the browser console now, the way\nsendToInstance() already does.","tree":{"sha":"e927a477d4d26a18d00f0676a6f82ce89aa54f62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/trees/e927a477d4d26a18d00f0676a6f82ce89aa54f62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/commits/2e7023bcc4eb2b5e2342200ee9fa8cd326fc0819","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/2e7023bcc4eb2b5e2342200ee9fa8cd326fc0819","node_id":"C_kwDOUPGd4toAKDJlNzAyM2JjYzRlYjJiNWUyMzQyMjAwZWU5ZmE4Y2QzMjZmYzA4MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d","sha":"ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d"}],"sha":"2e7023bcc4eb2b5e2342200ee9fa8cd326fc0819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/2e7023bcc4eb2b5e2342200ee9fa8cd326fc0819"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:02:02Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:04:49Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"message":"Put what is wrong with the release list under the list\n\nThe rate limit warning was rendered among the upload messages, below the\n\"Upload custom build\" heading - far from the field it is about. The other\nhalf of the same mistake was that a failed read of the list went into\nthis.state.error, the field that carries what went wrong with the upload,\nthe preparation or a delete.\n\nBoth now travel in one listStatus, with the severity attached, and are\nrendered directly under the field whose list they describe. error and\nnotice stay with the buttons, where what they report is done.\n\nThis also frees the green tick from the list: it hangs on the absence of\nan error, so a rate limit used to hide it even though the unpacked build\nit reports was perfectly fine.","tree":{"sha":"44826b86f6cd016bd7a92da1ffce9104b911dd5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/trees/44826b86f6cd016bd7a92da1ffce9104b911dd5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/commits/ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d","node_id":"C_kwDOUPGd4toAKGVhMmVkOTNmNTY2ODBhNDVmOGM1ZTllMWYyZTNlNjhhOThmZGFmMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2","sha":"4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2"}],"sha":"ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/ea2ed93f56680a45f8c5e9e1f2e3e68a98fdaf0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T08:46:58Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:04:49Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"message":"Name the GitHub rate limit instead of showing its status code\n\nThe settings dialog reads the release list straight from the GitHub API,\nover the address of the workstation and therefore on its own quota of\nsixty unauthenticated requests an hour. When it runs out, the dialog said\n\"could not load the CometVisu releases: GitHub returned 403\" in red - no\ncause, and no hint that nothing is broken: the uploaded archives stay\nusable and the configured version keeps being served.\n\nGitHub lists the counters in its access-control-expose-headers, so the\nbrowser may read them. A 403 or 429 with x-ratelimit-remaining at zero is\nnow reported as a warning that names the limit and, from\nx-ratelimit-reset, the time it lifts. Every other 403 stays an error -\nthe API answers with one for other reasons too.\n\nThe warning is set and cleared by the reading of the list alone, not by\nwhatever the user did last: it describes the state of the list, so\nuploading an archive in the meantime must not make it disappear.","tree":{"sha":"3b8934985a78169443dcc709a793d60462616a27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/trees/3b8934985a78169443dcc709a793d60462616a27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/commits/4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2","node_id":"C_kwDOUPGd4toAKDRkNjFiYzZlN2NiMTllYTE5ZjA4YmQ1MGJlYTViZGFiMjg5ZmM0YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b","sha":"a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b"}],"sha":"4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/4d61bc6e7cb19ea19f08bd50bea5bdab289fc4b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T08:30:35Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:04:49Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"message":"Give both version fields the width they need\n\n\"Serve through this web instance\" filled two thirds of the panel for the\nsake of \"web.0\". It is a built-in jsonConfig item, so the only lever is\nthe column count, and its help text shares the cell - four columns is as\nnarrow as it gets before that text turns into five lines.\n\nThe field above it followed its own content instead of its cell. It now\ntakes the width of a four-column cell exactly: in a twelve-column grid\nwith a 16px gutter, eight columns are twice four plus one gutter, so half\nof its cell minus half a gutter is the same width. The status display\nstarts right where the neighbouring column would, and no longer takes\nthat width away from the field.","tree":{"sha":"721b127dc0479409757e3916f582a0eedd970cb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/trees/721b127dc0479409757e3916f582a0eedd970cb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/commits/a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b","node_id":"C_kwDOUPGd4toAKGE3ZTU0MGRiYTg2OGZjZTQ4MmYzMTAzNDI2OTU2MzUzNGQ4YmU3M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commit/0ef5e9bcbb3ae4d74afbe3dde5e10bb820aef772","sha":"0ef5e9bcbb3ae4d74afbe3dde5e10bb820aef772","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/0ef5e9bcbb3ae4d74afbe3dde5e10bb820aef772"}],"sha":"a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/a7e540dba868fce482f31034269563534d8be73b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/commits/0ef5e9bcbb3ae4d74afbe3dde5e10bb820aef772/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T08:30:01Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:04:49Z","email":"jolt@tuxbox.org","name":"Florian Schirmer"},"message":"Prepare the CometVisu build when it is chosen, not when the adapter starts\n\nThe adapter asked the GitHub API on every start, even when the selected\nrelease had long been unpacked: ensureRelease() resolved the release\nbefore it looked at the .complete marker. That spent one of the sixty\nunauthenticated requests an hour and address for nothing, and a rate\nlimit or an unreachable GitHub kept the instance from serving a build\nthat was already on disk.\n\nThe release list is read where it was needed anyway - the settings dialog\n- and the archive it picks is handed to the adapter, which downloads and\nunpacks it there and then. A start only looks at the disk. What is left\nof the GitHub client is downloading one URL, and that URL is checked\nagainst the project''s own release downloads before anything is fetched.\n\nAn uploaded archive is unpacked the moment it arrives, for the same kind\nof reason: uploading one under a name it already had left the\nconfiguration untouched, so nothing restarted the instance and the build\nof the previous archive stayed in use.\n\nThe dialog shows the phases while the adapter works, and a tick once the\nselected version lies unpacked on the server - which it asks the adapter\nabout rather than deriving it from whatever happened last. Its own texts\nare translated now; \"Delete\", \"Select file\" and \"upload\" reuse words the\nadmin already ships, so they are not defined twice.\n\nClosing the dialog asks the adapter to drop the releases that were only\ntried out. Picking one fetches it at once, so looking around in the list\nleaves downloads behind that nothing would ever serve.\n\nAlso drops the handling of a \"latest\" selection. No released version\ncould write it: it was already legacy in 0.0.1 and appeared in no dialog.","tree":{"sha":"e0bb7d2950c0abd153e154427a7486cb84f81c5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/trees/e0bb7d2950c0abd153e154427a7486cb84f81c5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joltcoke/ioBroker.cometvisu/git/commits/0ef5e9bcbb3ae4d74afbe3dde5e10bb820aef772","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11374987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joltcoke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/joltcoke","id":11374987,"login":"joltcoke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzc0OTg3","organization